00 = 309,111.\n\nTherefore, the product of 493 and 627 is 309,111. Let me just verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0493  \nx627  \n----------\n\nFirst, multiply 493 by 7: 3451  \nThen multiply 493 by 20 (shift one position): 9860  \nThen multiply 493 by 600 (shift two positions): 295800  \nAdd them up as before. Which is exactly what I did. So the total is indeed 309,111.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check using a calculator method. Wait, since I can't use a calculator, perhaps do a quick check with estimation. 493 is close to 500, and 627 is close to 600. 500*600=300,000. The actual numbers are a bit less than 500 and a bit more than 600. 493 is 7 less, so 500-7, and 627 is 600+27. So (500-7)*(600+27) = 500*600 +500*27 -7*600 -7*27. Compute that:\n\n500*600=300,000  \n500*27=13,500  \n7*600=4,200  \n7*27=189  \nSo total is 300,000 +13,500 = 313,500; minus (4,200 +189)=4,389.  \n313,500 -4,389 = 309,111. Exactly the same result. So that confirms it. Therefore, the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 493 and 627 is \\boxed{309111}.\n"]
