 and multiply each part by 611 separately, then sum the results.\n\n1. Multiply 611 by the ones place digit (7):\n   \\[\n   611 \\times 7 = 4277\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 611 by the tens place digit (10):\n   \\[\n   611 \\times 10 = 6110\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 611 by the hundreds place digit (100):\n   \\[\n   611 \\times 100 = 61100\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n4277 + 6110 + 61100\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 4277 and 6110:\n\\[\n4277 + 6110 = 10387\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to 61100:\n\\[\n10387 + 61100 = 71487\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 611 and 117 is \\(\\boxed{71487}\\).",
