he answer is correct. So the steps are as outlined.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 657 and 847 is \\boxed{556479}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 657 and 847?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 847 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps:\n1. Multiply 657 by the ones place digit (7) of 847:\n   \\[\n   657 \\times 7 = 4599\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 657 by the tens place digit (40) of 847:\n   \\[\n   657 \\times 40 = 26280\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 657 by the hundreds place digit (800) of 847:\n   \\[\n   657 \\times 800 = 525600\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n4599 + 26280 + 525600 = 556479\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{556479}.",
