0, so 370×17 ≈ 6,290. Adding that to 333,000 gives 339,290. That matches. So the estimation also lines up. So I think that's correct.\n\nAlright, so the steps are:\n\n1. Multiply 370 by 7 (ones place): 2,590\n\n2. Multiply 370 by 10 (tens place): 3,700\n\n3. Multiply 370 by 900 (hundreds place): 333,000\n\nSumming them: 2,590 + 3,700 = 6,290; 6,290 + 333,000 = 339,290. So the final answer is 339,290.\n\nI think that's solid. Let me just make sure there's no arithmetic error in the steps. 370×7: 370×7. 300×7=2100, 70×7=490. 2100+490 is indeed 2590. 370×10 is 3700. 370×900: 370×9 is 3,330, so times 100 is 333,000. All correct. The addition steps are correct. So yeah, confident that 339,290 is the right answer.\n"]  2%|2         | 11/500 [09:18<6:51:11, 50.45s/it]
