inal answer should be 125,492.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 548 and 229 is \\boxed{125492}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 548 and 229, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of 229:\n\n1. **Multiply 548 by the ones place digit (9):**\n   \\[\n   548 \\times 9 = 4932\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(500 \\times 9 = 4500\\), \\(48 \\times 9 = 432\\), then \\(4500 + 432 = 4932\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 548 by the tens place digit (20):**\n   \\[\n   548 \\times 20 = 10960\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(548 \\times 2 = 1096\\), then \\(1096 \\times 10 = 10960\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 548 by the hundreds place digit (200):**\n   \\[\n   548 \\times 200 = 109600\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(548 \\times 2 = 1096\\), then \\(1096 \\times 100 = 109600\\).\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   4932 + 10960 + 109600 = 125492\n   \\]\n   - Step-by-step addition:\n     - \\(4932 + 10960 = 15892\\)\n     - \\(15892 + 109600 = 125492\\)\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{125492}\\).",
