90 x 8)\n      71100   (790 x 90, shifted one position to the left)\n    +790000   (790 x 100, shifted two positions to the left)\n    ------------\n      156420\n\nWait a second, in the vertical method, when multiplying by the hundreds place (1 in 198), it's 1*790 = 790, but since it's the hundreds place, it should be 790*100 = 79,000, so written as 79000. But in the way I wrote above, it's written as 790000? Wait, that's a mistake. Wait, no, let me check again. \n\nWait, no, when you write it vertically:\n\n          790\n        x198\n        -------\n          6320   (790 * 8)\n         71100   (790 * 90, which is the 9 in the tens place)\n        79000    (790 * 100, which is the 1 in the hundreds place)\n        ---------\n        Summing these:\n\n6320 + 71,100 = 77,420; plus 79,000 gives 156,420. So I think in my previous vertical notation, I mistakenly added an extra zero in the last line, but the actual calculation is correct. \n\nTherefore, all methods converge to 156,420. I think that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\n",
