it down into hundreds, tens, and ones places.\n1. Multiply 280 by the ones place digit (9) of 259:\n   \\[\n   280 \\times 9 = 2520\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 280 by the tens place digit (50) of 259:\n   \\[\n   280 \\times 50 = 14000\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 280 by the hundreds place digit (200) of 259:\n   \\[\n   280 \\times 200 = 56000\n   \\]\n\nSum all the step results:\n\\[\n2520 + 14000 + 56000 = 72520\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{72520}.",
