iplied by 50 (which is 5 in the tens place, so actually shifted one position to the left, so 280*5*10=14,000)\n\n280 multiplied by 200 (2 in the hundreds place, shifted two positions left, so 280*2*100=56,000)\n\nAdding all three gives 2520 +14,000=16,520; 16,520 +56,000=72,520. All methods confirm the same result. Therefore, I think the product is indeed 72,520. I don't see any errors in the calculations. So the answer should be 72,520.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 280 and 259 is \\boxed{72520}.\n"]
