=6  \nHundred thousands:2 +0=2. Wait, maybe better:\n\n240,600 is 240 thousand and 600. 25,263 is 25 thousand and 263. So total thousands: 240 +25 =265 thousands. The remaining 600 +263 =863. So total is 265,863. Yes, that's correct. So the final answer should be 265,863. I think that's right. Let me try another method, maybe using distributive property differently.\n\nAlternatively, 401 ×663 can be written as (400 +1) × (600 +60 +3). Expanding this:\n\n400×600 +400×60 +400×3 +1×600 +1×60 +1×3.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n400×600=240,000  \n400×60=24,000  \n400×3=1,200  \n1×600=600  \n1×60=60  \n1×3=3  \n\nAdding all these up:\n\n240,000 +24,000 =264,000  \n264,000 +1,200 =265,200  \n265,200 +600=265,800  \n265,800 +60=265,860  \n265,860 +3=265,863.\n\nSame result. Okay, so that confirms it. So the product is definitely 265,863. So the answer is correct.\n"]
