 use another method like distributive property.\n\nAlternatively, let me do 526 × 957 using another method to cross-verify.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator-like step:\n\nBut since I can't use a calculator, perhaps do 526 × 957:\n\nFirst, note that 526 × 1000 = 526,000. So subtract 43×526 (since 957 is 1000-43).\n\nWait, 957 = 1000 - 43. So 526×(1000-43) = 526,000 - (526×43).\n\nCalculating 526×43:\n\n526 ×40 = 21,040.\n\n526 ×3 = 1,578.\n\nAdding them: 21,040 + 1,578 = 22,618.\n\nSubtract that from 526,000: 526,000 -22,618 = 503,382.\n\nSame result! So that confirms that the product is indeed 503,382.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 503,382. Let me check the previous partial products again to ensure.\n\nFirst partial: 3,682.\n\nSecond: 26,300.\n\nThird: 473,400.\n\nAdding them: 3,682 +26,300 =29,982.\n\n29,982 +473,400: 29,982 +473,400 = 503,382. Yep, matches. So all steps are correct.\n\nI think that's thorough. The answer is 503,382.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 526 and 957 is \\boxed{503382}.\n"]
