on into three steps.\n1. Multiply 971 by the ones place digit (0) of 650:  \n   \\(971 \\times 0 = 0\\)\n2. Multiply 971 by the tens place digit (50) of 650:  \n   \\(971 \\times 50 = 48550\\)\n3. Multiply 971 by the hundreds place digit (600) of 650:  \n   \\(971 \\times 600 = 582600\\)\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(0 + 48550 + 582600 = 631150\\).\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{631150}\\).",
