t of 901 and 848, we break down the multiplication step by step using the digits of 848 (hundreds, tens, and ones places):\n\n1. **Multiply 901 by the ones place digit (8):**\n   \\[\n   901 \\times 8 = 7208\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 901 by the tens place digit (40):**\n   \\[\n   901 \\times 40 = 901 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 3604 \\times 10 = 36040\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 901 by the hundreds place digit (800):**\n   \\[\n   901 \\times 800 = 901 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 7208 \\times 100 = 720800\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results from the steps above:\n\\[\n7208 + 36040 + 720800\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the first two steps:\n\\[\n7208 + 36040 = 43248\n\\]\n\nThen, add this result to the third step's result:\n\\[\n43248 + 720800 = 764048\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 901 and 848 is \\(\\boxed{764048}\\).",
