 correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe another way to check the multiplication. Let me try multiplying 322 by 683 directly using another method, perhaps the standard algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 322 × 683:\n\nFirst, write them down:\n\n      322  \n    ×683  \n    -------\n    \nStarting with the ones digit of 683, which is 3:\n\n322 ×3 = 966 (as before)\n\nThen the tens digit is 8 (but it's actually 80, so we'll shift one position to the left):\n\n322 ×8 = 2576, then add a zero to make it ×80, so 25,760.\n\nThen the hundreds digit is 6 (actually 600, so shift two positions):\n\n322 ×6 =1,932, then add two zeros to make ×600, so 193,200.\n\nNow add those three results:\n\n966  \n25,760  \n193,200  \n--------\nTotal: 219,926. Same result. So that checks out.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 322 ×683 using another method, like breaking down the numbers differently. For instance, 683 can be written as 700 -17. Wait, but maybe that complicates. Alternatively, 322 × (700 -17) = 322×700 -322×17. Let me see if that works.\n\n322 ×700 is 322×7×100. 322×7: 300×7=2100, 20×7=140, 2×7=14. Total 2100+140=2240 +14=2254. ×100 is 225,400.\n\nThen 322×17. Let's compute that. 322×10=3,220; 322×7=2,254. Adding those gives 3,220 +2,254 =5,474. \n\nSo 225,400 -5,474 = ?\n\n225,400 minus 5,000 is 220,400. Then subtract 474 more: 220,400 -474 =219,926. \n\nSame result again. So that confirms it's 219,926. \n\nHmm, so I think that's correct. \n\nAnother way: use the standard vertical multiplication again, step by step.\n\n       322  \n     ×683  \n     --------\n        966   (322 ×3)  \n      25760   (322 ×80)  \n    +193200   (322 ×600)  \n    -------------\n      219,926  \n\nYes, adding those three gives 219,926. \n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 219,926.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 322 and 683 is \\boxed{219926}.\n"] 16%|#6        | 82/500 [1:10:59<7:05:35, 61.09s/it]
