e any mistakes in the calculations. So the final answer is 612,625.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 725 and 845 is \\boxed{612625}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 725 and 845?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 845 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps:\n1. Multiply 725 by the ones place digit 5 of 845:  \n   \\( 725 \\times 5 = 3625 \\).\n2. Multiply 725 by the tens place digit 40 of 845:  \n   \\( 725 \\times 40 = 29000 \\).\n3. Multiply 725 by the hundreds place digit 800 of 845:  \n   \\( 725 \\times 800 = 580000 \\).\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\( 3625 + 29000 + 580000 = 612625 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{612625}.",
