0 +636 =89,676. That matches.\n\nAlternatively, 636 \u00d7141. Let's see:\n\n636 \u00d7100 =63,600\n\n636 \u00d740 =25,440\n\n636 \u00d71 =636\n\nAdding those: 63,600 +25,440 =89,040; plus 636 gives 89,676. Same answer. So that's good.\n\nTherefore, I think the product is 89,676.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 141 and 636 is \\boxed{89676}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 141 and 636, we break down the multiplication by each place value of 636:\n\n1. **Multiply 141 by the ones place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   141 \\times 6 = 846\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - \\(100 \\times 6 = 600\\)\n   - \\(40 \\times 6 = 240\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 6 = 6\\)\n   - Sum: \\(600 + 240 + 6 = 846\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 141 by the tens place digit (30):**\n   \\[\n   141 \\times 30 = 4230\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - \\(141 \\times 3 = 423\\)\n   - \\(423 \\times 10 = 4230\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 141 by the hundreds place digit (600):**\n   \\[\n   141 \\times 600 = 84600\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - \\(141 \\times 6 = 846\\)\n   - \\(846 \\times 100 = 84600\\)\n\n**Summing all the results:**\n\\[\n846 + 4230 + 84600 = 89676\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 141 and 636 is \\(\\boxed{89676}\\).",
