d step: 264\u00d7500=132,000. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 1,584 +13,200 =14,784. Then 14,784 +132,000. 132,000 +14,000 is 146,000, plus 784 is 146,784. All steps check out. I think that's the correct answer. So the final product should be 146,784.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 264 and 556 is \\boxed{146784}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 264 and 556?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 556 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps.\n1. Multiply 264 by the ones place digit (6) of 556:\n   \\[\n   264 \\times 6 = 1584\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 264 by the tens place digit (50) of 556:\n   \\[\n   264 \\times 50 = 13200\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 264 by the hundreds place digit (500) of 556:\n   \\[\n   264 \\times 500 = 132000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n1584 + 13200 + 132000 = 146784\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{146784}.",
