rnatively, 264 ×556. Let me see if I can compute this as (200 +64) ×556.\n\n200×556 = 111,200\n\n64×556. Let's compute 64×500 =32,000; 64×56= 3,584 (since 64×50=3,200 and 64×6=384; 3,200+384=3,584). So 32,000 +3,584 =35,584. Then total is 111,200 +35,584 =146,784. Yep, same answer again. So that's good.\n\nTherefore, the product is 146,784. Let me check once more for any possible arithmetic errors. Let's see:\n\nFirst step: 264×6=1,584. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 264×50. 264×5=1,320, so 1,320×10=13,200. Correct.\n\nThird step: 264×500=132,000. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 1,584 +13,200 =14,784. Then 14,784 +132,000. 132,000 +14,000 is 146,000, plus 784 is 146,784. All steps check out. I think that's the correct answer. So the final product should be 146,784.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 264 and 556 is \\boxed{146784}.\n"]
