final_output:  ["\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 790 and 879?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 879 has three digits, so we can break it down into hundreds, tens, and ones places.\n1. Multiply 790 by the ones place digit 9 of 879:\n   \\[\n   790 \\times 9 = 7110\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 790 by the tens place digit 70 of 879:\n   \\[\n   790 \\times 70 = 55300\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 790 by the hundreds place digit 800 of 879:\n   \\[\n   790 \\times 800 = 632000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n7110 + 55300 + 632000 = 694410\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{694410}.", "662,410 + 32,000? Wait, no. Wait, 632,000 plus 62,410 is 694,410? Wait, no, wait. Wait, 632,000 + 60,000 is 692,000, then plus 2,410 is 694,410? Hmm, but wait let me check again.\n\nWait, 632,000 + 55,300 + 7,110. Wait, maybe I miscalculated the first addition. Let me recalculate:\n\nFirst part: 7,110 + 55,300 = 62,410. Then adding 632,000: 62,410 + 632,000. Let me add 62,410 + 600,000 first, which is 662,410. Then add the remaining 32,000? Wait, no, 632,000 is 600k + 32k. Wait, actually, 632,000 is 600,000 + 32,000. So 62,410 + 600,000 is 662,410, plus 32,000 would be 694,410? Wait, but that seems high. Let me check again step by step.\n\nWait, perhaps I made an error in splitting the numbers. Let me verify each step again.\n\nFirst, 790 × 879.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do this another way to cross-verify.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n       790\n     ×879\n     -------\n       790 × 9 = 7,110 (this is the ones place)\n      790 ×70 = 55,300 (tens place, shifted one position to the left)\n    790 ×800 = 632,000 (hundreds place, shifted two positions to the left)\n    -------------------\n    Now adding them up:\n    7,110\n    55,300\n    632,000\n    ---------\n    Let's add the first two: 7,110 +55,300 = 62,410. Then 62,410 +632,000 = 694,410.\n\nWait, so that's 694,410. But let me check with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property differently?\n\nAlternatively, 790 ×879 = 790 ×(800 +70 +9) = 790×800 +790×70 +790×9, which is exactly what I did. So that's correct. So the total is 632,000 + 55,300 +7,110 = ?\n\nAdding 632,000 and 55,300 first: 632,000 +55,300 = 687,300. Then add 7,110: 687,300 +7,110 = 694,410. Yes, that's the same.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach: 790 ×879. Let me think if there's a smarter way. For instance, 790 is 800 -10. So 800×879 -10×879. Let's see if that works.\n\nCalculating 800 ×879 first: 800×800 is 640,000, but no, wait 800×879 = 800*(800 +79) = 800×800 +800×79. Wait, 800×800 is 640,000. 800×79: 800×70=56,000; 800×9=7,200. So 56,000+7,200=63,200. So total 640,000 +63,200=703,200. Then subtract 10×879=8,790. So 703,200 -8,790 = ?\n\n703,200 minus 8,000 is 695,200. Then subtract 790 more: 695,200 -790 = 694,410. That's the same result. So that confirms it. So the answer is 694,410.\n\nHmm, so maybe my initial calculation was correct. But let me check again the first multiplication steps just to be thorough.\n\nFirst step: 790 ×9. 700×9=6,300. 90×9=810. 6,300+810=7,110. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 790×70. 700×70=49,000. 90×70=6,300. So total 49,000+6,300=55,300. Correct.\n\nThird step: 790×800. 700×800=560,000. 90×800=72,000. 560k +72k=632,000. Correct.\n\nAdding those together: 7,110 +55,300=62,410. Then +632,000 gives 694,410. Yes, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do the multiplication vertically:\n\n       790\n     ×879\n     -------\n       7110   (790 ×9)\n      55300   (790 ×70, shifted one position left)\n    632000    (790 ×800, shifted two positions left)\n    -----------\n    694,410\n\nYes, that adds up. So the answer is definitely 694,410. I think that's solid. Let me just check with a calculator approach mentally. Since 790×800 is 632,000, and then adding 790×79 (since 879 is 800+79). Wait, maybe that complicates, but let's see:\n\nWait, 790×879 = 790×(800 +70 +9) as before. Alternatively, 790×879 = (800 -10)×879 = 800×879 -10×879 = 703,200 -8,790 = 694,410. So same as before. \n\nAlternatively, approximate to check. 800×800 is 640,000, but our numbers are a bit higher. 800×900 would be 720,000. Since 790 is slightly less than 800 and 879 is slightly less than 900, so 790×879 should be a bit less than 720,000. Wait, but our answer is 694,410, which is indeed less. Alternatively, 800×879 is 703,200. So subtracting 10×879 gives 703,200-8,790=694,410. That's correct.\n\nI think I've verified it multiple ways, so I'm confident the product is 694,410.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 790 and 879 is \\boxed{694410}.\n"] 22%|##2       | 110/500 [1:35:31<7:10:42, 66.26s/it]
