swer.\n\nTherefore, the product is indeed 100,740. So I think that's the correct answer. Let me just recap the steps as per the template provided.\n\nThe question asks for the product of 292 and 345. Following the reasoning steps:\n\n1. Multiply 292 by the ones place digit (5) of 345, which is 292 \u00d75 =1,460.\n\n2. Multiply 292 by the tens place digit (40) of 345, which is 292 \u00d740 =11,680.\n\n3. Multiply 292 by the hundreds place digit (300) of 345, which is 292 \u00d7300 =87,600.\n\nThen, sum all those results: 1,460 +11,680 +87,600 =100,740.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 100,740. All steps check out with multiple methods, so I'm confident in the answer.\n</think>\n\n",
