83 as (500 +60) ×583 = 500×583 +60×583.\n\nLet me try that approach to check:\n\nFirst, 500 ×583. 500×500=250,000; 500×80=40,000; 500×3=1,500. So total 250,000 +40,000 =290,000 +1,500 =291,500. Wait, no, actually, wait. Wait, no, that's not correct. Wait, 500×583 is just 500 multiplied by the entire 583. Let me compute it directly:\n\n500 ×583 = 583 ×5 ×100 = 2915 ×100 =291,500. Okay, that's correct.\n\nThen 60 ×583. Let's compute that. 60×500=30,000; 60×80=4,800; 60×3=180. Adding those together: 30,000+4,800=34,800 +180=34,980. So total 291,500 +34,980 = 326,480. Same answer again. Okay, so that's good. So the result is consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method: 560 ×583.\n\nLet me think of 560 as 56×10, so 56×10 ×583 =56 ×583 ×10. Let me compute 56 ×583 first.\n\n56 ×583. Hmm, that might be a bit more involved, but let's try.\n\nBreakdown 583 into 500 +80 +3.\n\n56×500 = 28,000.\n\n56×80 = 4,480.\n\n56×3 = 168.\n\nAdding those: 28,000 +4,480 =32,480 +168 =32,648.\n\nThen multiply by 10: 326,480. Same answer. So that works too.\n\nAlright, so all methods are leading me to 326,480. So I think that's the correct product. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Let me just check once more with a calculator-like approach.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps using the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n\u202f\xa0560\n\n×583\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 560 by 3: 1680\n\nThen multiply 560 by 80 (which is 560×8 shifted one position): 4480 → 44800\n\nThen multiply 560 by 500 (shifted two positions): 280000\n\nAdd them up:\n\n1680\n\n+44800\n\n= 46480? Wait, no, wait. Wait 1680 +44,800 is 46,480? Wait no, that can't be. Wait, no, 1680 +44,800 is 46,480? Wait, no, no. Wait, 44,800 plus 1,680 is 46,480? Wait, no, 44,800 plus 1,680 would be 46,480. But then adding the 280,000?\n\nWait, no, I think I made a mistake here in the addition steps. Wait, no, in my first calculation I had:\n\nFirst part: 1,680\n\nSecond part:44,800\n\nThird part:280,000\n\nSo adding all three together: 280,000 +44,800 is 324,800, then adding 1,680 gives 326,480. That's correct.\n\nBut if I add the first two first, 1,680 +44,800 =46,480, then add to 280,000: 280,000 +46,480 = 326,480. Same result. Okay, so that's correct.\n\nI think I was confused for a moment there, but all right, the total is 326,480.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 326,480. I think that's solid. I've checked it multiple ways, so I'm confident.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 560 and 583 is \\boxed{326480}.\n"] 25%|##4       | 123/500 [1:46:04<5:40:29, 54.19s/it]
