ing those two: 7220 + 72200 = 79,420. Yep, same as before.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that 361 multiplied by 220 is 79,420.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 361 and 220 is \\boxed{79420}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 361 and 220?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 220 has three digits, so we can break it down into its place values (hundreds, tens, and ones):\n1. Multiply 361 by the ones place digit (0) of 220:  \n   \\(361 \\times 0 = 0\\)\n2. Multiply 361 by the tens place digit (20) of 220:  \n   \\(361 \\times 20 = 7220\\)\n3. Multiply 361 by the hundreds place digit (200) of 220:  \n   \\(361 \\times 200 = 72200\\)\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(0 + 7220 + 72200 = 79420\\).\n\nAnswer:  \nThe final computed product is \\boxed{79420}.",
