ltiplication way step by step to double-check.\n\nWriting it out:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0361  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0x220  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0------  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0000\xa0 (361 x 0)  \n\xa0\xa0\xa07220\xa0\xa0 (361 x 20, shifted one position to the left)  \n72200\xa0\xa0\xa0 (361 x 200, shifted two positions to the left)  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0------  \nAdding them up:\n\nThe first line is 0 (since 0 times 361 is 0, but written as 000).  \nSecond line: 7220 (from the tens place, which is 20).  \nThird line: 72200 (from the hundreds place, which is 200).  \nAdding those two: 7220 + 72200 = 79,420. Yep, same as before.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that 361 multiplied by 220 is 79,420.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 361 and 220 is \\boxed{79420}.\n"]
