</think>\n\nTo find the product of 615 and 793, we break down the multiplication step by step based on the digits of 793:\n\n1. **Multiply 615 by the ones place digit (3):**\n   \\[\n   615 \\times 3 = 1845\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 615 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   615 \\times 90 = 615 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 5535 \\times 10 = 55350\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 615 by the hundreds place digit (700):**\n   \\[\n   615 \\times 700 = 615 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 4305 \\times 100 = 430500\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n1845 + 55350 + 430500\n\\]\n\nAdding step by step:\n\\[\n1845 + 55350 = 57195\n\\]\n\\[\n57195 + 430500 = 487695\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 615 and 793 is \\(\\boxed{487695}\\).",
