0\n\n488,000 + 27,000 = 515,000\n\n515,000 + 2,100 = 517,100\n\n517,100 + 180 = 517,280. \n\nSame result again. So that's a good check. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator verification? Well, since I can't use a calculator, but let me see if I can compute 530*976 another way. Maybe break down 976 into 1000 - 24. So, 976 = 1000 - 24. Then, 530*(1000 - 24) = 530*1000 - 530*24 = 530,000 - 12,720. \n\nCalculating 530,000 minus 12,720. Let's do that:\n\n530,000 - 10,000 = 520,000\n\n520,000 - 2,720 = 517,280. \n\nSame answer again! Okay, so that confirms it. \n\nTherefore, after multiple methods, I can be confident that the product of 530 and 976 is 517,280. All the different approaches led to the same result, so that's reassuring. I think that's solid. \n\nJust to recap the original step-by-step as per the template: \n\n1. Multiply 530 by 6 (the ones place) to get 3,180.\n\n2. Multiply 530 by 70 (the tens place) to get 37,100.\n\n3. Multiply 530 by 900 (the hundreds place) to get 477,000.\n\nAdding them all together: 3,180 + 37,100 = 40,280; then 40,280 + 477,000 = 517,280. \n\nYep, that's exactly what I did. So the answer should be 517,280. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations here. All the cross-checking methods align, so I think that's the correct product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 530 and 976 is \\boxed{517280}.\n"]
