 those together: 4,360 +981 = 5,341. Then multiply by 10 gives 53,410. That matches the previous result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, another way: 109 ×490.\n\nBut let me also try the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n\u2003\xa0109\n\n×490\n\n________\n\nFirst, multiply 109 by 0 (the ones place of 490), which gives 0. Then multiply 109 by 9 (the tens place, which is actually 90), so shifted one position to the left:\n\n109 ×9 = 981, so written as 9810.\n\nThen multiply 109 by 4 (the hundreds place, which is 400), so shifted two positions to the left:\n\n109 ×4 = 436, so written as 43600.\n\nNow, add the two results: 9810 +43600 = 53,410. Exactly the same as before. So that confirms it.\n\nHmm, so the final answer should be 53,410.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with calculator math. Since I can't use a calculator, but maybe approximate?\n\n100 × 490 = 49,000. Then 9 ×490 = 4,410. So adding those gives 49,000 +4,410 =53,410. Yes! That's another way: 109 is 100 +9. So (100+9)×490 = 100×490 +9×490 = 49,000 +4,410 =53,410. Perfect, that's the same answer. So that confirms it again.\n\nTherefore, I think the correct product is 53,410. I don't see any errors in the steps now. All different methods lead to the same result. So I can be confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 109 and 490 is \\boxed{53410}.\n"]
