her method, perhaps breaking down both numbers:\n\n967 is 900 + 60 +7  \n692 is 600 + 90 +2  \n\nMultiplying using the distributive property:\n\n(900+60+7)*(600+90+2) = 900*600 + 900*90 + 900*2 + 60*600 + 60*90 +60*2 +7*600 +7*90 +7*2  \n\nCalculating each term:\n\n900*600 = 540,000  \n900*90 = 81,000  \n900*2 = 1,800  \n60*600 = 36,000  \n60*90 = 5,400  \n60*2 = 120  \n7*600 = 4,200  \n7*90 = 630  \n7*2 =14  \n\nNow adding all these up:\n\nStart with the largest terms:\n\n540,000 + 81,000 = 621,000  \n621,000 +1,800 = 622,800  \n622,800 +36,000 = 658,800  \n658,800 +5,400 = 664,200  \n664,200 +120 = 664,320  \n664,320 +4,200 = 668,520  \n668,520 +630 = 669,150  \n669,150 +14 = 669,164.  \n\nAgain, same result. So definitely the answer is 669,164. \n\nTherefore, the step-by-step partial products method was correct. The initial calculation had the right partial products and their sum. So I think that's solid. \n\nJust to recap:\n\nFirst partial (2): 1,934  \nSecond partial (90): 87,030  \nThird partial (600): 580,200  \nTotal: 1,934 + 87,030 = 88,964; 88,964 +580,200 = 669,164. \n\nYes, all checks out. No mistakes detected in the reasoning steps. So the final answer should be 669,164.\n</think>\n\n",
