 by 6: 1968.\n\nMultiply 328 by 30: 9840.\n\nMultiply 328 by 600: 196800.\n\nAdding those gives 1968 +9840 =11808, plus 196,800 gives 208,608. Yes, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made a mistake in the initial addition steps? Let me check again.\n\nFirst partial product: 1968.\n\nSecond: 9840.\n\nThird: 196800.\n\nAdding first two: 1968 + 9840. 1968 + 9000 is 10968, plus 840 is 11808. Then adding 196,800 to that. 11808 + 196,800. Let's break it down: 196,800 + 10,000 =206,800; then 206,800 +1,808 =208,608. Yep, that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another approach: 328 × 636 = 328 × (600 + 36) = 328×600 + 328×36. Let's compute 328×36 first.\n\n328 ×36: 328×30=9,840 and 328×6=1,968. Adding those gives 9,840 +1,968 =11,808. Then add to 196,800 (which is 328×600). 196,800 +11,808 =208,608. So same result.\n\nOkay, so I think that's the correct answer. Let me just confirm once more with a different method. Let's compute 328 ×636 as:\n\n(300 +28) × (600 +36) = 300×600 + 300×36 +28×600 +28×36.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n300×600 = 180,000.\n\n300×36 = 10,800.\n\n28×600 =16,800.\n\n28×36: 28×30=840 and 28×6=168, so total 840+168=1,008.\n\nAdding all four terms:\n\n180,000 +10,800 =190,800.\n\n190,800 +16,800 =207,600.\n\n207,600 +1,008 =208,608.\n\nSame result! Okay, so that's definitely correct. Therefore, the final product is 208,608.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 328 and 636 is \\boxed{208608}.\n"]
