s compute that.\n\n900 *423: 9*423 = 3,807, so 900*423 is 380,700.\n\n2*423 = 846.\n\nSo, subtracting: 380,700 - 846 = 380,700 - 800 = 379,900, then subtract 46 more: 379,900 -46 = 379,854. That matches the previous result. So that's good. So that confirms that the answer is 379,854.\n\nTherefore, the product of 898 and 423 is 379,854.\n\nWait, but let me make sure that in my first calculation, when I broke down the multiplication steps, I didn't make any errors. Let me check the individual partial products again.\n\nFirst partial product: 898 * 3. 898 *3. 800*3=2400, 90*3=270, 8*3=24. 2400+270 is 2670, plus 24 is 2694. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 898 *20. 898*2 is 1,796, so times 10 gives 17,960. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 898*400. 898*4 is 3,592, times 100 is 359,200. Correct.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n2694 +17,960 = 20,654; 20,654 +359,200 = 379,854. All correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using a calculator method here. Wait, since I can't use a calculator, but perhaps do another verification. Let's see:\n\nLet me compute 898 *423 step by step:\n\nStarting with 898 × 3 = 2,694.\n\nThen 898 × 20 = 17,960 (as before).\n\nThen 898 ×400 = 359,200 (as before).\n\nAdding all gives 2,694 +17,960 = 20,654; 20,654 +359,200 = 379,854. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another approach, like multiplying 423 by 898.\n\nLet me reverse the multiplication: 423 × 898.\n\nBreaking down 898 into 800 +90 +8.\n\nSo, 423×800 = 338,400.\n\n423×90 = 38,070 (since 423×9=3,807, so times 10 is 38,070).\n\n423×8 = 3,384.\n\nAdding those: 338,400 +38,070 = 376,470; then +3,384 = 379,854. Same result again.\n\nOkay, so that's a good sign. All methods are leading me to the same answer. So I think the product is indeed 379,854.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 379,854. I'll make sure to present it in the required format with the steps.\n"]
