80.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 915 and 292 is \\boxed{267180}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 915 and 292, we break down the multiplication step by step using the digits of 292:\n\n1. **Multiply 915 by the ones place digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   915 \\times 2 = 1830\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 915 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   915 \\times 90 = 915 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 8235 \\times 10 = 82350\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 915 by the hundreds place digit (200):**\n   \\[\n   915 \\times 200 = 915 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 1830 \\times 100 = 183000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the intermediate results:\n\\[\n1830 + 82350 + 183000\n\\]\n\nAdding step by step:\n\\[\n1830 + 82350 = 84180\n\\]\n\\[\n84180 + 183000 = 267180\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{267180}\\).",
