 292 is 300 -8). So 274,500 - (915 ×8). Let's compute 915 ×8: 900×8=7,200, 15×8=120, so total 7,320. Then subtract: 274,500 -7,320 = 267,180. So same result. Okay, that confirms it.\n\nTherefore, the final product should be 267,180.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, let me check each step again:\n\nFirst step: 915 ×2 = 1,830. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 915 ×90. 915×9 is 8,235, so ×10 is 82,350. Correct.\n\nThird step: 915 ×200. 915×2 is 1,830, ×100 is 183,000. Correct.\n\nAdding 1,830 +82,350 = 84,180. Then 84,180 +183,000 = 267,180. All steps check out. So I think that's the right answer.\n\nI don't see any errors in my calculations. So I can confidently say the product is 267,180.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 915 and 292 is \\boxed{267180}.\n"]
