culating each term:\n\n273 ×300 = 81,900  \n273 ×30 = 8,190  \nSubtracting: 81,900 -8,190 = 73,710. \n\nSame answer again. So that's good. \n\nAlternatively, using the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n     273  \n   ×270  \n   -------\n     000   (273 ×0, since the ones place is 0)\n   19110   (273 ×70, shifted one position to the left)\n  54600    (273 ×200, shifted two positions to the left)\n   -------\n   73710\n\nAdding those lines: 000 +19110 =19110, plus 54600 gives 73710. \n\nTherefore, all methods confirm that the product is 73,710. \n\nI think that's solid. So the answer should be 73,710. \n\nWait, just to be absolutely sure, maybe I can use a calculator method here. Since I can't use a calculator, but let me do another step-by-step. \n\nMultiplying 273 by 270:\n\nFirst, note that 273 × 270 = 273 × 27 × 10. \n\nCompute 273 ×27:\n\n273 ×20 = 5,460  \n273 ×7 = 1,911  \nAdding them gives 5,460 +1,911. Let's see:\n\n5,460 +1,000 =6,460  \n6,460 +911 =7,371. \n\nYes, so 7,371 ×10 is 73,710. \n\nAlright, that's consistent again. \n\nSo I think I can confidently say the answer is 73,710. \n\nWait, just to check if there was any miscalculation in partial products:\n\nOriginal breakdown:\n\nOnes place: 273 ×0 =0  \nTens place: 273 ×70 =19,110  \nHundreds place: 273 ×200=54,600  \n\nSum: 0 +19,110 =19,110; 19,110 +54,600. \n\nLet me add 19,110 +54,600 again. \n\n19,110 +54,600:\n\n19,110 +50,000 =69,110  \n69,110 +4,600 =73,710. \n\nYes, that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, 19,110 +54,600:\n\n19,110  \n+54,600  \n=73,710 (since 19+54=73 for the ten thousands and thousands, and 110+600=710 for the hundreds and below). \n\nYep. \n\nTherefore, all steps are correct. So the answer is definitely 73,710. \n\nI think that's thorough. I considered multiple methods to verify, so I can be sure there's no mistake.\n\n"]
