 14,532; then 14,532 + 69,200 = 83,732. Yep, consistent.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 692 \u00d7 121 directly step by step:\n\nFirst, write down the multiplication:\n\n\u2003\u2003692  \n\u00d7\u00a0121  \n________  \n\u2003\u2003692  (this is 692 \u00d7 1)  \n\u20031384\u2003 (this is 692 \u00d7 2, but shifted one position) but wait, actually when multiplying by the tens digit, it's 2, so 692 \u00d72 is 1384, but since it's the tens place, it's actually 13840. Hmm, maybe I need to write it properly.\n\nWait, in the standard algorithm:\n\nWhen you multiply by the tens digit (2 in the tens place, so 20), you write the result shifted one to the left, so it becomes 13,840. Similarly, the hundreds digit (1 in the hundreds place, so 100) gives 69,200 shifted two places.\n\nSo adding those three lines gives the total. \n\nAlternatively, to check with a calculator approach, if I can do the multiplication step by step:\n\n692 \u00d7 121.\n\nLet me compute 692 \u00d7 100 = 69,200.\n\n692 \u00d7 20 = 13,840.\n\n692 \u00d7 1 = 692.\n\nAdding those three together: 69,200 + 13,840 = 83,040; 83,040 + 692 = 83,732. \n\nEverything checks out. So the final answer should be 83,732. I think that's correct. I don't see any mistakes in the steps. Let me just confirm once again with another method. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the fact that 121 is 11\u00d711, so 692\u00d711\u00d711. Let's see:\n\nFirst compute 692 \u00d7 11. 692 \u00d710 is 6,920 plus 692 is 7,612. Then multiply that by 11 again: 7,612 \u00d711. \n\nCalculating 7,612 \u00d710 =76,120 plus 7,612 gives 83,732. Yep, same result. \n\nThat's a good cross-verification. So that's another way to do it. So that confirms the answer is correct. \n\nTherefore, the product of 692 and 121 is indeed 83,732.\n</think>\n\n",
