e that, maybe 736 × 9 first, then multiply by 10. 736 × 9: 700×9=6300, 36×9=324. So 6300+324=6624. Then times 10 is 66,240. Wait, but in the example, they just wrote "Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153". So maybe they just do 27 ×50 directly. So same here, 736 ×90 would be the second step.\n\n3. Multiply 736 by the hundreds digit, which is 6, but in the hundreds place, so 600. So 736 ×600. Let\'s see, 736 ×6 = 4,416, then times 100 is 441,600.\n\nThen sum all three results: 5,888 + 66,240 + 441,600. Let me add them step by step. First, 5,888 + 66,240. Let\'s add 5,888 + 60,000 = 65,888, then add 6,240: 65,888 +6,240 = 72,128. Then add that to 441,600: 72,128 + 441,600. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is ']]
