tively, maybe compute 666 * 960 as 666 * (1000 - 40) = 666*1000 - 666*40. Let me see if that gives the same result.\n\n666*1000 = 666,000\n\n666*40 = 26,640\n\nSo 666,000 - 26,640 = ?\n\n666,000 - 20,000 = 646,000\n\nThen subtract 6,640 more: 646,000 - 6,640 = 639,360. Oh, same result. So that confirms it.\n\nTherefore, the product should be 639,360. Let me check once more with a calculator method.\n\nAlternatively, 666 * 960:\n\nMultiply 666 by 960.\n\nFirst, 666 * 960 = 666 * (9.6 * 100) = (666 * 9.6) * 100.\n\nCalculating 666 * 9.6:\n\n666 * 9 = 5994\n\n666 * 0.6 = 399.6\n\nAdding them: 5994 + 399.6 = 6393.6\n\nMultiply by 100 gives 639,360. Yep, that matches.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the correct product is 639,360.\n\nWait, but in the initial step-by-step reasoning, when I broke down 666*60 as 39960, that's correct because 666*6=3996, times 10 gives 39960. And 666*900=599,400. Adding those gives 639,360. So all methods lead to the same answer. Therefore, the final answer is 639,360.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 666 and 960 is \\boxed{639360}.\n"]
