ld check once more with a calculator approach, but since I can't use a calculator, let me verify with another method. \n\nAlternatively, let me compute 271 × 797 step by step again:\n\n271 × 7 = 1,897  \n271 × 90 = 24,390  \n271 × 700 = 189,700  \nAdding them: 1,897 +24,390 =26,287; 26,287 +189,700=215,987. Yep, same.\n\nAlternatively, adding in a different order: 189,700 +24,390 =214,090; then +1,897 gives 215,987. \n\nOkay, so that seems consistent. Therefore, the answer should be 215,987. \n\nWait, but let me check if I multiplied 271 ×90 correctly. 271 ×9 is 2,439, so adding a zero gives 24,390. Correct. And 271×7 is 1,897. Correct. 271×700 is 189,700. Correct. \n\nSo all steps are correct. Therefore, the final answer is 215,987. \n\nI think that's solid. Maybe I made a mistake in adding once, but since two different methods give the same result, I can be confident. \n\nFinal check: Let me see, 270 ×800 would be 216,000. Since 271 is 1 more than 270, and 797 is 3 less than 800, so the difference would be (270 ×800) + (1×800) - (270×3) - (1×3). \n\nWait, that's the expansion of (270+1)*(800-3). Let me compute that:\n\n270×800 = 216,000  \n270×(-3) = -810  \n1×800 = 800  \n1×(-3) = -3  \nTotal: 216,000 -810 +800 -3 = 216,000 -10 -3 = 215,987. \n\nSame result again. So that's a fourth method confirming. Okay, definitely correct. \n\nTherefore, the answer is 215,987.\n\n"]
