reds place) which is 700, so 353*7 is 2,471, shifted two positions to the left (i.e., 247,100).\n\nThen adding all three: 1,765 +17,650 +247,100 = 266,515. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method: (350 +3)*(700 +50 +5). Let's expand this.\n\n350*700 = 245,000\n\n350*50 = 17,500\n\n350*5 = 1,750\n\n3*700 = 2,100\n\n3*50 = 150\n\n3*5 = 15\n\nNow add all these:\n\n245,000 +17,500 = 262,500\n\n262,500 +1,750 = 264,250\n\n264,250 +2,100 = 266,350\n\n266,350 +150 = 266,500\n\n266,500 +15 = 266,515. \n\nSame result! Okay, so that's a good cross-verification. So I think the answer is 266,515. \n\nTherefore, the final product should be 266,515. I think that's correct. Let me just do a quick check using approximate estimation to see if it's reasonable. 350*750 is 262,500. Since 353 is 3 more than 350 and 755 is 5 more than 750, so the extra would be 3*750 + 350*5 + 3*5. Which is 2,250 + 1,750 +15 = 4,015. So adding that to 262,500 gives 266,515. Perfect, that's exactly the same. So that confirms it. \n\nTherefore, the answer is 266,515.\n\n"]
