9 first. 900×9 is 8,100, 28×9 is 252. Adding those gives 8,100 + 252 = 8,352. Then multiply by 100 to get 835,200. Wait, because 900 is 9×100, so 928×9×100. So yes, that's 835,200. So the third partial product is 835,200. This should be shifted two places to the left, so it's 835,200.\n\nNow, adding all three partial products together:.\n\nFirst:     4,640.\nSecond:   64,960.\nThird: 835,200.\n\nAdding the first two: 4,640 + 64,960 = 69,600. Then adding that to 835,200 gives 69,600 + 835,200. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
