ect.\n\nSecond step: 140\u00d720. 140\u00d72=280, so times 10 is 2800. Correct.\n\nThird step: 140\u00d7100=14,000. Correct.\n\nSum: 980 +2800= 3780. Then 3780 +14,000=17,780. Correct.\n\nAlright, so the answer is 17,780. I think that's solid. Let me just write it in the required format now.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 140 and 127 is \\boxed{17780}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 140 and 127?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 127 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 140 by the ones place digit 7 of 127:  \n   \\(140 \\times 7 = 980\\).\n2. Multiply 140 by the tens place digit 20 of 127:  \n   \\(140 \\times 20 = 2800\\).\n3. Multiply 140 by the hundreds place digit 100 of 127:  \n   \\(140 \\times 100 = 14000\\).\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(980 + 2800 + 14000 = 17780\\).\n\nSo, the final computed product is 17780.\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 140 and 127 is \\boxed{17780}.",
