130-3. Hmm, but maybe that's more complicated. Let's see: 140×130 - 140×3. 140×130: 140×100=14,000; 140×30=4,200; total is 18,200. Then subtract 140×3=420, so 18,200 -420=17,780. Yep, that also works. So all methods are giving me the same result, so I think that's correct.\n\nTherefore, following the template structure, the steps would be as outlined. Let me just make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors in the initial steps. Let's recheck each multiplication:\n\nFirst step: 140 ×7. 140×7: 100×7 is 700, 40×7 is 280. 700+280=980. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 140×20. 140×2=280, so times 10 is 2800. Correct.\n\nThird step: 140×100=14,000. Correct.\n\nSum: 980 +2800= 3780. Then 3780 +14,000=17,780. Correct.\n\nAlright, so the answer is 17,780. I think that's solid. Let me just write it in the required format now.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 140 and 127 is \\boxed{17780}.\n"]
