      "text": "20,800 + 9,776. Let's add 20,000 + 9,000 = 29,000. Then 800 + 776 = 1,576. So total would be 29,000 + 1,576 = 30,576? Wait, no, that can't be right. Wait, maybe I should add them directly:\n\n20,800\n\n+ 9,776\n\n= ?\n\n20,800 + 9,000 is 29,800. Then add 776: 29,800 + 700 is 30,500, plus 76 is 30,576. Hmm, but let me check again because sometimes adding this way can lead to errors.\n\nAlternatively, 20,800 + 9,776:\n\n20,800 + 9,776:\n\n20,000 + 9,000 = 29,000\n\n800 + 776 = 1,576\n\nTotal is 29,000 + 1,576 = 30,576. Yes, that's the same.\n\nWait, but let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe multiplying 104 by 294 directly another way.\n\nAlternatively, 294 can be written as 300 - 6. So, 104*(300 -6) = 104*300 - 104*6.\n\n104*300 is 31,200. 104*6 is 624. So, 31,200 - 624 = 30,576. That matches the previous result. So that's good.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 30,576.\n\nBut let me check once more with standard multiplication:\n\n   104\n\nx294\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 104 by 4: 416\n\nThen 104 x90 (shift one position): 9,360\n\nThen 104 x200 (shift two positions): 20,800\n\nAdding those:\n\n416\n\n+9,360 = 9,776\n\n+20,800 = 30,576. Yep, same as before.\n\nSo the steps are correct. Therefore, the answer is 30,576.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 104 and 294 is \\boxed{30576}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 104 and 294?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 294 has three digits, so we can break it down into three steps:\n1. Multiply 104 by the ones place digit (4) of 294:\n   \\[\n   104 \\times 4 = 416\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 104 by the tens place digit (90) of 294:\n   \\[\n   104 \\times 90 = 9360\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 104 by the hundreds place digit (200) of 294:\n   \\[\n   104 \\times 200 = 20800\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n416 + 9360 + 20800 = 30576\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{30576}.",
