final_output:  ['\n\nTo find the product of 555 and 971, we can break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of the digits in 971.\n\n1. **Multiply 555 by the ones place digit (1):**\n   \\[\n   555 \\times 1 = 555\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 555 by the tens place digit (70):**\n   \\[\n   555 \\times 70 = 555 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 3885 \\times 10 = 38850\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 555 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   555 \\times 900 = 555 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 4995 \\times 100 = 499500\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n555 + 38850 + 499500\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the ones and tens place multiplications:\n\\[\n555 + 38850 = 39405\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to the hundreds place multiplication:\n\\[\n39405 + 499500 = 538905\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{538905}\\).', "538,500 + 405? Wait, no, maybe I miscalculated. Wait, 499,500 + 39,405:\n\n499,500 + 30,000 is 529,500. Then add 9,405 more: 529,500 +9,000 is 538,500, plus 405 is 538,905. Wait, that seems off. Wait, maybe I need to check again.\n\nWait, 499,500 + 39,405. Let's add them digit by digit:\n\n499,500\n\n+\xa0 39,405\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 +5 =5\n\n0 +0=0\n\n5 +4 =9 (the tens place)\n\n9 (hundreds place) +9 (from 39,405's hundreds digit is 4? Wait, hold on. Let me write it properly:\n\n499500\n\n+\xa0 39405\n\nAligning the numbers:\n\n499500\n\n+\xa0 39405\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n0 +5 =5\n\n0 +0 =0\n\n5 (third digit) +4 (second digit of 39405's thousands place?) Wait, maybe it's easier to write:\n\n499500 is:\n\n4 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones)\n\n39405 is:\n\n0 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 5 (ones)\n\nWait no, 39,405 is 3 (ten thousands?), no. Wait 39,405 is 3 (ten thousands place?), no, 39,405 is:\n\nDigit places:\n\n3 (ten thousands) is actually no,