 but let me check once more with another method. Let's do 927 \u00d7540 as (900 +27)(500 +40). Wait, expanding that:\n\nFirst, 900\u00d7500 = 450,000\n\n900\u00d740 = 36,000\n\n27\u00d7500=13,500\n\n27\u00d740=1,080\n\nAdding all those: 450,000 +36,000 = 486,000; 13,500 +1,080 =14,580. Then 486,000 +14,580 =500,580. Same result again. Okay, so I'm confident now.\n\nTherefore, the product of 927 and 540 is 500,580.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 927 and 540 is \\boxed{500580}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 927 and 540?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 540 has three digits, so we can break it down into its place values:\n1. Multiply 927 by the ones place digit (0) of 540:\n   \\[\n   927 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 927 by the tens place digit (40) of 540:\n   \\[\n   927 \\times 40 = 927 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 3708 \\times 10 = 37080\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 927 by the hundreds place digit (500) of 540:\n   \\[\n   927 \\times 500 = 927 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 4635 \\times 100 = 463500\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n0 + 37080 + 463500 = 500580\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{500580}.",
