40=4,860. So 4,860 ×100=486,000.\n\n27 ×540: 27×500=13,500 and 27×40=1,080. So total 13,500+1,080=14,580.\n\nAdding those together: 486,000 +14,580 = 500,580. Same result. Okay, so that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like multiplication:\n\n       927\n     ×540\n     -------\nFirst multiply by 0: 0000 (but shifted by 0 digits)\nThen multiply by 4 (tens place): 927×4=3,708, then shift one to the left: 37,080\nThen multiply by 5 (hundreds place): 927×5=4,635, then shift two to the left: 463,500\nAdd them all: 0 +37,080 +463,500 = 500,580.\n\nYes, that matches. So I think the answer is 500,580.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another method. Let's do 927 ×540 as (900 +27)(500 +40). Wait, expanding that:\n\nFirst, 900×500 = 450,000\n\n900×40 = 36,000\n\n27×500=13,500\n\n27×40=1,080\n\nAdding all those: 450,000 +36,000 = 486,000; 13,500 +1,080 =14,580. Then 486,000 +14,580 =500,580. Same result again. Okay, so I'm confident now.\n\nTherefore, the product of 927 and 540 is 500,580.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 927 and 540 is \\boxed{500580}.\n"]
