,510. Yes, that matches. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, using standard multiplication:\n\n   309\n\n× 390\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 309 ×0 =0 (written as 0000)\n\nThen multiply 309 ×9 (tens place, so actually 90, so shifted one position)\n\nWait, actually in standard multiplication:\n\nThe second number is 390, so first multiply by 0 (units place), giving 0.\n\nThen multiply by 9 (tens place), so 309×9=2781, shifted one position to the left (×10) → 27810.\n\nThen multiply by 3 (hundreds place), so 309×3=927, shifted two positions to the left (×100 → ×100 gives ×100, so 927×100=92,700).\n\nThen add all three: 0 +27,810 +92,700 = 120,510. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 120,510. So I think that's correct.\n\nWait, but let me just do straight multiplication:\n\n309 × 390.\n\nAlternatively, 309 × 39 ×10. Let's compute 309×39 first, then multiply by 10.\n\n309 ×39:\n\nBreakdown: 300×39 +9×39.\n\n300×39 = 11,700.\n\n9×39 = 351.\n\n11,700 +351 =12,051.\n\nThen multiply by10 gives 120,510. Yep, same result. Okay, so that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 309 and 390 is 120,510.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 309 and 390 is \\boxed{120510}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 309 and 390, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of 390.\n\n1. **Multiply 309 by the ones place digit (0):**\n   \\[\n   309 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 309 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   309 \\times 90 = 309 \\times 9 \\times 10\n   \\]\n   Calculate \\(309 \\times 9\\):\n   \\[\n   300 \\times 9 = 2700 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 9 \\times 9 = 81\n   \\]\n   Adding these results:\n   \\[\n   2700 + 81 = 2781\n   \\]\n   Then multiply by 10:\n   \\[\n   2781 \\times 10 = 27810\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 309 by the hundreds place digit (300):**\n   \\[\n   309 \\times 300 = 309 \\times 3 \\times 100\n   \\]\n   Calculate \\(309 \\times 3\\):\n   \\[\n   300 \\times 3 = 900 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 9 \\times 3 = 27\n   \\]\n   Adding these results:\n   \\[\n   900 + 27 = 927\n   \\]\n   Then multiply by 100:\n   \\[\n   927 \\times 100 = 92700\n   \\]\n\n**Summing all the results:**\n\\[\n0 + 27810 + 92700 = 120510\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 309 and 390 is \\(\\boxed{120510}\\)."] 42%|####2     | 210/500 [2:53:29<3:59:55, 49.64s/it]
