u00a0\u00a0 x952\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 --------\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 712\u00a0\u00a0 (356 x 2)\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 1780\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 (356 x 5, shifted one position to the left becomes 17800)\n\n\u00a0 3204\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 (356 x 9, shifted two positions left becomes 320400)\n\nThen add them:\n\n712 + 17800 = 18512; 18512 + 320400 = 338,912. So that matches.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 338,912.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with a calculator approach. Since I can't use a calculator, but maybe approximate.\n\n356 * 1000 would be 356,000. But 952 is 48 less than 1000. So, 356*(1000 - 48) = 356,000 - (356*48).\n\nCompute 356*48: 356*40 = 14,240 and 356*8 = 2,848. So total is 14,240 + 2,848 = 17,088.\n\nThus, 356,000 - 17,088 = 338,912. Exactly the same as before. So that confirms it's correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 338,912.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 356 and 952 is \\boxed{338912}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 356 and 952, we break it down into three steps based on the place values of the digits in 952:\n\n1. **Multiply 356 by the ones place digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   356 \\times 2 = 712\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 356 by the tens place digit (50):**\n   \\[\n   356 \\times 50 = 356 \\times 5 \\times 10 = 1780 \\times 10 = 17800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 356 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   356 \\times 900 = 356 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 3204 \\times 100 = 320400\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n712 + 17800 + 320400 = 338912\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 356 and 952 is \\(\\boxed{338912}\\).",
