r the template. So the final answer is 590,226.\n\nWait, but in the template, the user wrote \"sum of the results\" and the example had three steps for 153 (ones, tens, hundreds). Since 966 is also three digits, so three steps. The steps in the reasoning would be:\n\n1. Multiply 611 by 6 (ones place)\n\n2. Multiply 611 by 60 (tens place)\n\n3. Multiply 611 by 900 (hundreds place)\n\nThen sum all three. So the reasoning part should list those three steps. I think that's exactly what I did. So the answer is correct. Alright, I think that's solid.\n</think>\n\n",
