n\nFirst, write them down:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0744\n\n×\xa0259\n\n--------\n\nStart by multiplying 744 by 9 (the ones place):\n\n744 × 9: 700×9=6300; 44×9=396. 6300+396=6696. So that's 6,696.\n\nNext, multiply 744 by 50 (the tens place, which is 5×10):\n\n744 ×50 = 744 ×5 ×10. 744×5=3,720. ×10 gives 37,200. So that's 37,200 shifted one position to the left (since it's the tens place). But since we're writing it out, we just add a zero at the end, so 37,200.\n\nThen multiply by 200 (the hundreds place, which is 2×100):\n\n744 ×200 = 744×2×100 = 1,488 ×100 = 148,800. This is shifted two positions left, so written as is.\n\nNow, adding all three:\n\n6,696\n\n37,200\n\n148,800\n\nAdding them up:\n\n6,696 +37,200 =43,896 as before. Then 43,896 +148,800 =192,696. So that checks out.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method like the distributive property:\n\n744 ×259 =744 ×(200 +50 +9) =744×200 +744×50 +744×9 = same as before, so that gives the same result.\n\nAlternatively, to confirm, perhaps use a calculator approach. But since I can't use a calculator, maybe approximate to check if the answer is reasonable.\n\n744 is approximately 700, and 259 is approximately 250. 700×250=175,000. Our answer is 192,696 which is higher, but since we rounded down both numbers, the actual product should be higher. 700×250 is 175k, but 744 is 44 more than 700, so 44×250 =11,000, so 175k+11k=186k. Then 259 is 9 more than 250, so 700×9=6,300, so total 186k+6.3k=192.3k. Hmm, so 192,300, which is very close to our result of 192,696. The difference is because we approximated 744 as 700 and 259 as 250. The actual numbers are a bit higher, so the exact answer is 192,696, which is in the ballpark. So that seems reasonable.\n\nTherefore, I think the correct answer is 192,696.\n\n"]
