cting: 154,000 - 2,772 = 151,228. Yep, same result. So that\'s a good check. \n\nAlternatively, use the distributive property step by step. Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the user expects the breakdown as per each digit step-by-step, so the reasoning is presented in three steps, even if one of them is zero. Let me check the original template example given. In the example with 27 and 153, they had three steps: multiplying by 3 (ones), 50 (tens), and 100 (hundreds). Wait, 153 is 1 hundred, 5 tens, 3 ones. So for 308, which is 3 hundreds, 0 tens, 8 ones, so the steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 491 by 8 (ones place)\n2. Multiply 491 by 0 (tens place, so actually 0×10, but since it\'s the tens digit, it\'s 0×491×10)\n3. Multiply 491 by 3 (hundreds place, so 3×100×491)\n\nSo the steps as per the template would be:\n\n1. 491 × 8 = 3,928\n2. 491 × 0 (but shifted one place, so 0×10? Wait, the original example said "Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153". So in that case, the tens digit was 5, so they did 27×50. \n\nAh, right, so in the tens place, it\'s the digit times 10. So for 308\'s tens digit (0), it\'s 0×10, so 0. So the second step is 491 × (0×10) = 0. \n\nThird step is hundreds digit 3, so 3×100, so 491×300 = 147,300. \n\nThus, adding 3,928 + 0 + 147,300 = 151,228. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be 151,228. \n\nI think that\'s solid. Let me just confirm with a calculator-style multiplication:\n\n491 × 308:\n\nFirst, 491 × 8 = 3,928\n\nThen 491 × 0 (tens place) = 0, but written as 00 shifted one, so 00\n\nThen 491 ×3 (hundreds) = 1,473 shifted two places is 147,300\n\nAdd them: 3,928 + 0 + 147,300 = 151,228. Yep, that\'s correct.\n\nSo the final answer is 151,228. I think that\'s right. I don\'t see any mistakes in the steps. The key point was handling the zero in the tens place correctly, but since it\'s zero, that term drops out, so the sum is just the ones and hundreds place contributions. Alright, confident now.\n']
