 700, 922 is approximately 900. 700×900=630,000. The actual answer is 635,258, which is close to the estimate, so that makes sense. The slight difference is because we rounded up both numbers, so the actual product is a bit higher than 630,000. So that seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 689 ×922 as (700 -11) × (900 +22). But that might complicate, but let's see:\n\nWait, maybe expand using distributive property:\n\n(700 -11)(900 +22) =700×900 +700×22 -11×900 -11×22.\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n700×900=630,000.\n\n700×22=15,400.\n\n-11×900= -9,900.\n\n-11×22= -242.\n\nAdding all together: 630,000 +15,400 = 645,400; then minus 9,900 gives 635,500; then minus 242 gives 635,500 -242 =635,258. Exactly the same result! So that confirms it. So the answer is indeed 635,258.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, I'm confident the product of 689 and 922 is 635,258."]
