asoning follows that structure. \n\nIn the example, they did:\n\n1. Multiply by the ones digit (3), then the tens digit (50), then hundreds (100). \n\nSo for 166, the digits are 6 (ones), 6 (tens place which is 60), and 1 (hundreds place which is 100). \n\nSo the steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 340 by 6 (ones place)\n2. Multiply 340 by 60 (tens place)\n3. Multiply 340 by 100 (hundreds place)\nThen add all three. \n\nWhich is exactly what I did. So the steps are correct. \n\nTherefore, the final answer is 56,440. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 340 and 166 is \\boxed{56440}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 340 and 166?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 166 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 340 by the ones place digit 6 of 166:  \n   \\(340 \\times 6 = 2040\\).\n2. Multiply 340 by the tens place digit 60 of 166:  \n   \\(340 \\times 60 = 20400\\).\n3. Multiply 340 by the hundreds place digit 100 of 166:  \n   \\(340 \\times 100 = 34000\\).\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(2040 + 20400 + 34000 = 56440\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{56440}.",
