      "text": "268,223? Wait, maybe I messed up in the addition.\n\nWait, let me check again. Let's add 1,083 +14,440 first. 1,083 +14,440. 1,000 +14,000 is 15,000. 83 +440 is 523. So total 15,523. Then adding that to 252,700. Let's do 252,700 +15,523. 252,700 +10,000 =262,700. Then add 5,523 more: 262,700 +5,523 = 268,223. Hmm, okay, that seems right.\n\nWait a second, but let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   361\n\u00d7 743\n--------\n\nFirst, write them down:\n\n       361\n     \u00d7743\n     -------\nFirst multiply by 3 (ones place):\n\n3\u00d7361 = 1,083\n\nThen multiply by 4 (tens place, so shifted one position left):\n\n4\u00d7361 = 1,444 \u2192 but since it's the tens place, it's 14,440\n\nThen multiply by 7 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):\n\n7\u00d7361 = 2,527 \u2192 shifted two places is 252,700\n\nNow add them:\n\n1,083\n\n+14,440\n\n=15,523\n\n15,523 +252,700 =268,223. Okay, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 361\u00d7700 + 361\u00d740 +361\u00d73. Which is exactly what we did. So that's 252,700 +14,440 is 267,140, plus 1,083 is 268,223. Wait, hold on, 252,700+14,440 is 267,140? Let me check that again. 252,700 +14,440. 252,700 +10,000 is 262,700, plus 4,440 is 267,140. Then adding 1,083 gives 267,140 +1,083 =268,223. Yep, that's correct.\n\nHmm, so the final answer should be 268,223. Let me just cross-verify with another approach. Maybe using the distributive property: (300+60+1)(700+40+3). But that might be tedious, but let's see:\n\n300\u00d7700 = 210,000\n\n300\u00d740 =12,000\n\n300\u00d73 =900\n\n60\u00d7700 =42,000\n\n60\u00d740 =2,400\n\n60\u00d73 =180\n\n1\u00d7700 =700\n\n1\u00d740 =40\n\n1\u00d73 =3\n\nNow add all these up:\n\n210,000 +12,000 =222,000\n\n222,000 +900 =222,900\n\n222,900 +42,000 =264,900\n\n264,900 +2,400 =267,300\n\n267,300 +180 =267,480\n\n267,480 +700 =268,180\n\n268,180 +40 =268,220\n\n268,220 +3 =268,223. \n\nOkay, that matches! So that confirms it's 268,223. Phew. So the answer is correct. I think that's thorough. I made sure to check through different methods to be certain, especially since the numbers are a bit large and it's easy to make an addition error. But both the step-by-step multiplication and the expanded form gave the same result, so I feel confident now.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 361 and 743 is \\boxed{268223}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 361 and 743?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 743 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 361 by the ones place digit (3) of 743:\n   \\[\n   361 \\times 3 = 1083\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 361 by the tens place digit (40) of 743:\n   \\[\n   361 \\times 40 = 14440\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 361 by the hundreds place digit (700) of 743:\n   \\[\n   361 \\times 700 = 252700\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n1083 + 14440 + 252700 = 268223\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{268223}.",
