677 and 647?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 647 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 677 by the ones place digit 7 of 647: \n   \\[\n   677 \\times 7 = 4739\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 677 by the tens place digit 40 of 647:\n   \\[\n   677 \\times 40 = 27080\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 677 by the hundreds place digit 600 of 647:\n   \\[\n   677 \\times 600 = 406200\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n4739 + 27080 + 406200 = 438019\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{438019}\\).",
