ct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 410 and 351 is \\boxed{143910}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 410 and 351?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 351 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 410 by the ones place digit (1) of 351:\n   \\[\n   410 \\times 1 = 410\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 410 by the tens place digit (50) of 351:\n   \\[\n   410 \\times 50 = 20,\\!500\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 410 by the hundreds place digit (300) of 351:\n   \\[\n   410 \\times 300 = 123,\\!000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n410 + 20,\\!500 + 123,\\!000 = 143,\\!910\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{143910}.",
