 gives 143,500. Then add 410: 143,500 +410=143,910. Yep, same answer.\n\nSo seems like the product is indeed 143,910. I think that's correct. Let me check once more with calculator steps.\n\nAlternatively, 410 × 351:\n\nFirst, 400 × 351 = 140,400.\n\nThen 10 × 351 = 3,510.\n\nAdding those together: 140,400 + 3,510 = 143,910. Exactly the same. So that confirms it.\n\nOkay, so all methods lead to 143,910. I think that's the right answer. The reasoning steps as per the template would be the three multiplications and then adding them up. So the steps are correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 410 and 351 is \\boxed{143910}.\n"]
