ld be 99,408.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 114 and 872?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 872 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.  \n1. Multiply 114 by the ones place digit 2 of 872:  \n   \\( 114 \\times 2 = 228 \\).  \n2. Multiply 114 by the tens place digit 70 of 872:  \n   \\( 114 \\times 70 = 7,\\!980 \\).  \n3. Multiply 114 by the hundreds place digit 800 of 872:  \n   \\( 114 \\times 800 = 91,\\!200 \\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\( 228 + 7,\\!980 + 91,\\!200 = 99,\\!408 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **99,408**.",
