ps.\n1. Multiply 414 by the ones place digit (2) of 142:\n   \\[\n   414 \\times 2 = 828\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 414 by the tens place digit (40) of 142:\n   \\[\n   414 \\times 40 = 16,560\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 414 by the hundreds place digit (100) of 142:\n   \\[\n   414 \\times 100 = 41,400\n   \\]\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n828 + 16,560 + 41,400 = 58,788\n\\]\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{58788}.",
