ndard multiplication algorithm:\n\n       191\n     ×871\n     -------\n\nFirst multiply 191 by 1 (units place): 191.\n\nThen multiply 191 by 70 (tens place, which is 7 in the tens place, so ×7 then shift one position):\n\n191 ×7 = 1,337, written as 13,370.\n\nThen multiply 191 by 800 (hundreds place, so ×8 shifted two positions):\n\n191 ×8 =1,528, written as 152,800.\n\nAdding them up gives 191 +13,370 =13,561 +152,800 =166,361. So that seems consistent.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method to be absolutely sure. Maybe breaking down the numbers differently.\n\nAlternatively, use distributive property: (200 -9) × (800 +70 +1).\n\nWait, 191 is 200-9. Let me see if that helps.\n\nSo, (200 -9)(800 +70 +1) = 200*(800+70+1) -9*(800+70+1)\n\nCompute 200×800 =160,000; 200×70=14,000; 200×1=200. So total for 200 part: 160,000 +14,000 =174,000 +200 =174,200.\n\nThen subtract 9*(800+70+1). Compute 9×800=7,200; 9×70=630; 9×1=9. So total subtraction:7,200+630=7,830 +9=7,839.\n\nSo total is 174,200 -7,839.\n\nCompute 174,200 -7,000 =167,200; then subtract 839 more: 167,200 -800=166,400; then -39=166,361. Same result! Okay, so that confirms it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method: 191×871. Let me see if I can compute this mentally or with another breakdown.\n\nAlternatively, 191×871 = 191×(800 +70 +1). Wait, that's the same as before. Anyway, since two different methods give the same answer, I think 166,361 is correct.\n\nWait, but let me check with a calculator approach step by step.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 191×800 first, which is 152,800. Then 191×70=13,370. Then 191×1=191. Adding those: 152,800 +13,370 is 166,170. Then +191 gives 166,361. Yes, same answer. So I think that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 166,361.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 191 and 871 is \\boxed{166361}.\n"]
