thod. Let's see, 631 × 896.\n\nAlternatively, 631 × 900 = 567,900. Then subtract 631 ×4 = 2,524. So 567,900 -2,524 = 565,376. Oh, that works too. Let me check that:\n\n631 × 900 = 631 × 9 × 100 = 5,679 × 100 = 567,900.\n\nThen 631 ×4 = 2,524. So 567,900 -2,524 = ?\n\n567,900 minus 2,524:\n\nSubtract 2,000 first: 567,900 -2,000 = 565,900.\n\nThen subtract 524: 565,900 - 524 = 565,376. Yes, same result. So that confirms it.\n\nTherefore, the product is 565,376. I think that's correct. Let me just check with a calculator-style multiplication:\n\n631 ×896:\n\nLet me compute 631 × 800 = 504,800.\n\n631 ×90 = 56,790.\n\n631 ×6 =3,786.\n\nAdding all three: 504,800 +56,790 is 561,590? Wait, wait, no: 504,800 +56,790. Let me add that again: 504,800 +50,000 is 554,800, plus 6,790 is 561,590. Then adding 3,786: 561,590 +3,786 = 565,376. Yes, that's correct. So that's consistent. So the answer is 565,376.\n\nWait, just to ensure that I didn't make any arithmetic errors in the initial steps:\n\nFirst step: 631 ×6:\n\n600×6 =3600, 30×6=180, 1×6=6. 3600+180=3780+6=3786. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 631×90. 631×9=?\n\n600×9=5400, 30×9=270, 1×9=9. 5400+270=5670+9=5679. Then ×10 gives 56,790. Correct.\n\nThird step: 631×800. 631×8=?\n\n600×8=4800, 30×8=240, 1×8=8. 4800+240=5040+8=5048. ×100 → 504,800. Correct.\n\nAdding all three:\n\n3786 +56,790 =60,576. Then 60,576 +504,800 =565,376. All steps check out. So the final answer is 565,376.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe final computed product is \\boxed{565376}.\n"]
