is 2440. That checks out. .\n\nThird step, 122×100. Multiplying by 100 moves the decimal two places, so 122 becomes 12200. Correct. .\n\nNow, I need to add all these partial products together. Let's line them up properly:.\n\n   732.\n+ 2440.\n+12200.\n--------.\nLet me add the first two: 732 + 2440. 700 + 2400 is 3100, and 32 + 40 is 72. So 3100 + 72 = 3172. Then add that to 12200. 3172 + 12200. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
