e final product. \n\nAlternatively, if I do the multiplication the long way:\n\n      832\n    \u00d7 600\n    -------\n      0   (832 \u00d7 0)\n     0    (832 \u00d7 0, shifted one position)\n  4992    (832 \u00d76, shifted two positions)\n    -------\n  499200\n\nYes, adding those three lines (which are 0 + 0 + 499200) gives the total. \n\nTherefore, the answer is 499,200.\n</think>\n\n",
