r way. Let's use the standard algorithm step by step as written:\n\nMultiplying 263 by 361:\n\nFirst, write 263\n\n\u00d7 361\n\n________\n\nMultiply 263 by 1 (units place): 263.\n\nWrite that down.\n\nNext, multiply 263 by 6 (tens place). But since it's the tens place, the 6 represents 60. So, 263 \u00d76 is 1,578. But since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left, so it becomes 15,780.\n\nThen multiply 263 by 3 (hundreds place). The 3 is in the hundreds place, so it's 300. So, 263 \u00d73 is 789, then shift two positions to the left, making it 78,900.\n\nNow, adding all three results:\n\n263\n\n15,780\n\n78,900\n\nTotal:\n\nStart with 263 +15,780 = 16,043.\n\nThen 16,043 +78,900 = 94,943. Yep, same as before.\n\nAlright, I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in the steps. Therefore, the product of 263 and 361 is indeed 94,943. I think that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\n",
