 adding the zero gives 19,960. Wait, hold on, 499×4 is actually 1996? Let me check again. 400×4=1600, 90×4=360 (total so far 1960), plus 9×4=36, so 1960+36=1996. Yeah, so 1996×10 is 19,960. Okay, so second step is 19,960.\n\nThird step: 499 × 500. Since 500 is 5×100, maybe do 499×5 first then add two zeros. Let's compute 499×5. 400×5=2000, 90×5=450, 9×5=45. Adding those: 2000+450=2450, plus 45 is 2495. Then multiply by 100, so that's 249,500. .\n\nNow, I need to add all three results together: 1,497 + 19,960 + 249,500. Let me add the first two first. 1,497 + 19,960. Let's see, 1,497 + 19,960. Adding 1,497 + 20,000 would be 21,497, but since it's 19,960, that's 40 less. So 21,497 - 40 = 21,457. Wait, maybe better to do straight addition:.\n\n1,497  .\n+19,960  .\n=?.\n\nAdding the thousands: 1,000 + 19,000 = 20,000. Then the hundreds: 400 + 900 = 1,300. Tens: 90 + 60 = 150. Ones: 7 + 0 =7. Wait, maybe that's complicating. Alternatively:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1,497  .\n+19,960  .\nAligning digits:.\n\n  1,497  .\n+19,960  .\n=--------.\nLet's add units place: 7 +0=7  .\nTens: 9 +6=15, carry over 1  .\nHundreds:4 +9=13, plus the carried 1 makes 14, so 4 and carry 1  .\nThousands: 1 +9=10, plus carried 1 makes 11, so 1 and carry 1  .\nTen-thousands: 1 (from the 19,960's 1 in the ten-thousands place) plus the carried 1 gives 2. .\n\nWait, maybe I should write it properly:.\n\n19,960  .\n+\xa01,497  .\n=21,457. Yes, that's correct. So 19,960 +1,497 is 21,457.\n\nNow add that to the third part, 249,500. .\n\n21,457 + 249,500. Let's see, 21,457 + 200,000 = 221,457. Then add 49,500: 221,457 +49,500. .\n\n221,457 + 40,000 = 261,457. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
