git. Let me make sure that approach also gives the same result. \n\nBreaking down 750 into digits:\n\n- The ones digit is 0, so multiply 384 x0 = 0.\n\n- The tens digit is 5 (but since it's the tens place, it's 50). So 384 x50 = 19,200.\n\n- The hundreds digit is 7 (so 700). 384 x700 = 268,800.\n\nAdding those three partial products: 0 +19,200 +268,800 = 288,000. Perfect. \n\nTherefore, all methods lead to the same answer. I think that's thorough. \n\nJust to ensure there's no arithmetic mistake, let me re-calculate each partial product:\n\nFirst partial product: 384 x0 =0. Correct.\n\nSecond: 384 x50. 384x5=1,920. Then 1,920 x10 =19,200. Correct.\n\nThird: 384x700. 384x7=2,688. Then 2,688 x100 =268,800. Correct.\n\nAdding 19,200 +268,800:\n\n19,200 +268,800. Let's do 268,800 +19,200. Breaking it down: 268,800 + 20,000 =288,800, but since it's 19,200, subtract 800: 288,800 -800= 288,000. Yep, that's right.\n\nAlright, so confident now that the answer is 288,000.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 384 and 750 is \\boxed{288000}.\n"]
