wo zeros)\n     --------\n     444486\n\nYes, when adding those three partial products:\n\n5586\n+39900\n= 45486\n\n45486 + 399000 = 444,486. \n\nAll right, I think that's correct. I don't see any errors in the steps. So the product of 798 and 557 is 444,486.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 798 and 557 is \\boxed{444486}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 798 and 557, we break down 557 into its place values (500, 50, and 7) and multiply each by 798, then sum the results.\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place (7):**\n   \\[\n   798 \\times 7 = 5586\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   \\[\n   700 \\times 7 = 4900, \\quad 90 \\times 7 = 630, \\quad 8 \\times 7 = 56\n   \\]\n   Summing these:\n   \\[\n   4900 + 630 + 56 = 5586\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place (50):**\n   \\[\n   798 \\times 50 = 39900\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   \\[\n   798 \\times 5 = 3990 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 10)} \\quad 3990 \\times 10 = 39900\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place (500):**\n   \\[\n   798 \\times 500 = 399000\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   \\[\n   798 \\times 5 = 3990 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 100)} \\quad 3990 \\times 100 = 399000\n   \\]\n\n**Summing all the results:**\n\\[\n5586 + 39900 + 399000 = 444486\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 798 and 557 is \\(\\boxed{444486}\\).",
