t:\n\n911 \u00d7 8:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1 (units digit) \u00d78 =8\n\nNext digit: 1 (tens place) \u00d78 =8, but since it's the tens place, it's 80, so written as 8 in the tens place.\n\nThen the hundreds digit: 9 \u00d78=72, so 7200.\n\nAdding those: 7000 + 200 + 80 +8? Wait, no, wait:\n\nWait, 911 is 9 hundreds, 1 ten, 1 unit. \n\nSo 9 (hundreds) \u00d78 =72 hundreds =7200,\n\n1 (tens) \u00d78 =8 tens=80,\n\n1 (units) \u00d78=8 units,\n\nSo total is 7200 +80 +8 =7288. That's correct.\n\nThen 911 \u00d7300: 911 \u00d73 \u00d7100. 911\u00d73 is 2733, so times 100 is 273,300. Correct.\n\nAdding them gives 273,300 +7,288. Let me add again step by step:\n\n273,300 +7,000 = 280,300,\n\nThen add the remaining 288: 280,300 +200 =280,500,\n\nthen +88 is 280,588. Correct.\n\nHmm, seems consistent. So I think that's the right answer. \n\nI don't see any errors in the steps. So the final product should be 280,588.\n</think>\n\n",
