 (504-500)=4 and (800-791)=9. So the difference would be 500\u00d79 (4,500) minus 4\u00d7791 (3,164), so net difference 1,336. So that matches. Therefore, confident it's correct.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 504 and 791?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 791 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 504 by the ones place digit (1):  \n   \\(504 \\times 1 = 504\\).\n2. Multiply 504 by the tens place digit (90):  \n   \\(504 \\times 90 = 504 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 4,\\!536 \\times 10 = 45,\\!360\\).\n3. Multiply 504 by the hundreds place digit (700):  \n   \\(504 \\times 700 = 504 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 3,\\!528 \\times 100 = 352,\\!800\\).\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(504 + 45,\\!360 + 352,\\!800 = 398,\\!664\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **398,664**.",
