oken down into steps for each digit of number2 (since number2 has three digits, so three steps). Let me structure it as per the template.\n\nOriginal template example:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 27 and 153?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 27 by the ones place digit 3 of 153: 27\u00d73=81\n2. Multiply 27 by the tens place digit 50 of 153: 27\u00d750=1350\n3. Multiply 27 by the hundreds place digit 100 of 153: 27\u00d7100=2700\nAnswer: Now, sum all the step results: 81 + 1350 + 2700 = 4131. So the final product is 4131.\n\nSo following that structure, for the current problem with 135 and 591, the reasoning should be similar.\n\nBreaking down 591 into 500 (hundreds), 90 (tens), and 1 (ones). So the steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 135 by the ones digit (1): 135\u00d71=135\n2. Multiply 135 by the tens digit (90): 135\u00d790=12,150\n3. Multiply 135 by the hundreds digit (500): 135\u00d7500=67,500\n\nThen sum all three results: 135 + 12,150 + 67,500 = ?\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\nFirst, 135 + 12,150 = 12,285\n\nThen, 12,285 + 67,500 = 79,785. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 79,785. I think that's right. Let me just confirm once more with a calculator approach.\n\nAlternatively, multiplying 135 \u00d7591:\n\nLet me compute 135 \u00d7591:\n\nFirst, multiply 135 \u00d7 500 = 67,500\n\nThen 135 \u00d790 = 12,150\n\nThen 135 \u00d71 =135\n\nAdding them gives 67,500 +12,150 = 79,650; then +135 = 79,785. Yes, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n\u2003\u2003\u2003135  \n\u00d7\u202f\u00a0591  \n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \n\u2003\u2003135 \u00d7 1 = 135  \n\u2003135 \u00d7 90 = 12,150 (shifted one position)  \n135 \u00d7500 =67,500 (shifted two positions)  \nAdding them up gives the total. Yep, that's the same as before.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 79,785. I don't see any mistakes in the steps now. 