\nTo find the product of 209 and 826, we can break down the multiplication step by step using the standard algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 209 by the ones place digit (6) of 826:**\n   \\[\n   209 \\times 6 = 1254\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(200 \\times 6 = 1200\\) and \\(9 \\times 6 = 54\\), so \\(1200 + 54 = 1254\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 209 by the tens place digit (20) of 826:**\n   \\[\n   209 \\times 20 = 4180\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(209 \\times 2 = 418\\), then shift one position to the left (multiply by 10) gives \\(4180\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 209 by the hundreds place digit (800) of 826:**\n   \\[\n   209 \\times 800 = 167200\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(209 \\times 8 = 1672\\), then shift two positions to the left (multiply by 100) gives \\(167200\\).\n\n**Sum all the partial products:**\n\\[\n1254 + 4180 + 167200\n\\]\n\n- First, add \\(1254\\) and \\(4180\\):\n  \\[\n  1254 + 4180 = 5434\n  \\]\n\n- Then add the result to \\(167200\\):\n  \\[\n  5434 + 167200 = 172634\n  \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 209 and 826 is \\(\\boxed{172634}\\).",
