g with the distributive method shows the same result, so I can be confident.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 712 and 839 is \\boxed{597368}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 712 and 839?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 839 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 712 by the ones place digit 9 of 839:\n   \\[\n   712 \\times 9 = 6408\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 712 by the tens place digit 30 of 839 (shifted one position to the left):\n   \\[\n   712 \\times 30 = 21360\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 712 by the hundreds place digit 800 of 839 (shifted two positions to the left):\n   \\[\n   712 \\times 800 = 569600\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n6408 + 21360 + 569600 = 597368\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{597368}.",
