horough. Maybe I made an error in multiplying 149 by 8. Let's check that again:\n\n149 \u00d78:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n100 \u00d78 = 800\n\n40 \u00d78 = 320\n\n9 \u00d78 =72\n\nAdding those: 800 + 320 = 1,120; 1,120 +72= 1,192. Yes, so 149\u00d78 is 1,192. Then times 100 (since it's 800) gives 119,200. Correct.\n\n149 \u00d73: 100\u00d73=300; 40\u00d73=120; 9\u00d73=27. 300+120=420; 420+27=447. So 447, then times 10 gives 4,470. Correct.\n\n149\u00d71 is 149. Adding all together:\n\n119,200 + 4,470 = 123,670; then +149 gives 123,819. Yep.\n\nAlright, I think that's solid. So the answer is 123,819. I don't see any mistakes in the steps. The cross-verification using the approximation method also gave the same result, so I feel confident that this is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 149 and 831 is \\boxed{123819}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 149 and 831, we break down the multiplication using the place values of 831 (which is a three-digit number):\n\n1. Multiply 149 by the ones place digit (1) of 831:\n   \\[\n   149 \\times 1 = 149\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 149 by the tens place digit (30) of 831:\n   \\[\n   149 \\times 30 = 149 \\times 3 \\times 10 = 447 \\times 10 = 4470\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 149 by the hundreds place digit (800) of 831:\n   \\[\n   149 \\times 800 = 149 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 1192 \\times 100 = 119200\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n149 + 4470 + 119200\n\\]\n\nAdding these step-by-step:\n\\[\n149 + 4470 = 4619\n\\]\n\\[\n4619 + 119200 = 123819\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{123819}\\).",
