0. That matches.\n\nThird, multiply by 300 (hundreds place). So 3×6 is 18, write 8 carryover 1.\n\n3×6 is 18 +1=19, write 9 carryover1.\n\n3×6 is 18 +1=19. So the third partial product is 1986, shifted two places to the left, making it 198,600. Correct.\n\nAdding all together:\n\n3972\n\n+33100\n\n+198600\n\n= 235,672.\n\nHmm, seems consistent. Alternatively, maybe check with another method, like using distributive property: (600+60+2)(300+50+6). But that might be more complicated, but let's try.\n\nExpanding (a+b+c)(d+e+f) = ad + ae + af + bd + be + bf + cd + ce + cf. So:\n\n600×300 = 180,000\n\n600×50 = 30,000\n\n600×6 = 3,600\n\n60×300 = 18,000\n\n60×50 = 3,000\n\n60×6 = 360\n\n2×300 = 600\n\n2×50 = 100\n\n2×6 = 12\n\nNow add all these up:\n\nStart with 180,000 +30,000 =210,000\n\n+3,600 →213,600\n\n+18,000 →231,600\n\n+3,000 →234,600\n\n+360 →234,960\n\n+600 →235,560\n\n+100 →235,660\n\n+12 →235,672.\n\nYes! That's the same result. So that confirms it. The product is indeed 235,672. Therefore, I think the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe final computed product is \\boxed{235672}.\n"]
