 final answer is 476,982. I think that's solid.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 657 and 726 is \\boxed{476982}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 657 and 726?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 726 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 657 by the ones place digit 6 of 726:  \n   \\(657 \\times 6 = 3942\\).\n2. Multiply 657 by the tens place digit 20 of 726:  \n   \\(657 \\times 20 = 13140\\).\n3. Multiply 657 by the hundreds place digit 700 of 726:  \n   \\(657 \\times 700 = 459900\\).\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(3942 + 13140 + 459900 = 476982\\).\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{476982}.",
