maybe do 228 ×449 as (200 +28) ×(400+40+9). But that might complicate, but let me try expanding:\n\n(200 + 28)(400 +40 +9) = 200×400 + 200×40 +200×9 +28×400 +28×40 +28×9.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n200×400 = 80,000.\n\n200×40 = 8,000.\n\n200×9 = 1,800.\n\n28×400 = 11,200.\n\n28×40 = 1,120.\n\n28×9 = 252.\n\nAdding all these up:\n\n80,000 +8,000 =88,000.\n\n88,000 +1,800 =89,800.\n\n89,800 +11,200 =101,000.\n\n101,000 +1,120 =102,120.\n\n102,120 +252 =102,372. Yep, same result. So that confirms it.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 102,372.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 228 and 449 is \\boxed{102372}.\n"] 68%|######7   | 339/500 [4:38:17<2:03:42, 46.10s/it]
