lly, when multiplying by the ones digit, the first partial product is 4104 as before.\n\nNext, multiply by 8 (tens place). Since it's the tens digit, we shift one position to the left. So:\n\n8\u00d74=32, write 2, carry 3.\n\n8\u00d78=64 +3=67, write 7 carry 6.\n\n8\u00d76=48 +6=54, write 4 and carry 5. Since there are no more digits, write the 5. So the second partial product is 54720 (with a zero at the end because of the shift).\n\nThen multiply by 4 (hundreds place), shifted two positions:\n\n4\u00d74=16, write 6 carry 1.\n\n4\u00d78=32 +1=33, write 3 carry 3.\n\n4\u00d76=24 +3=27, write 7 and carry 2. Then write the 2. So that gives 2736, but shifted two places becomes 273600.\n\nAdding them all:\n\n4104\n\n54720\n\n273600\n\nTotal:\n\n4104 +54720 = 58824.\n\n58824 +273600 = 332,424.\n\nSame result again. Okay, so that must be correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 684 and 486 is 332,424.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 684 and 486 is \\boxed{332424}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 684 and 486, we use the standard multiplication method step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 684 by the ones place digit (6) of 486:**\n   \\[\n   684 \\times 6 = 4104\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(6 \\times 4 = 24\\) (write 4, carry 2)\n     - \\(6 \\times 8 = 48 + 2 = 50\\) (write 0, carry 5)\n     - \\(6 \\times 6 = 36 + 5 = 41\\) (write 41)\n\n2. **Multiply 684 by the tens place digit (80) of 486:**\n   \\[\n   684 \\times 80 = 54720\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(8 \\times 4 = 32\\) (write 2, carry 3)\n     - \\(8 \\times 8 = 64 + 3 = 67\\) (write 7, carry 6)\n     - \\(8 \\times 6 = 48 + 6 = 54\\) (write 54)\n     - Shift one position to the left (multiply by 10)\n\n3. **Multiply 684 by the hundreds place digit (400) of 486:**\n   \\[\n   684 \\times 400 = 273600\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(4 \\times 4 = 16\\) (write 6, carry 1)\n     - \\(4 \\times 8 = 32 + 1 = 33\\) (write 3, carry 3)\n     - \\(4 \\times 6 = 24 + 3 = 27\\) (write 27)\n     - Shift two positions to the left (multiply by 100)\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   4104 + 54720 + 273600 = 332424\n   \\]\n   - Step-by-step addition:\n     - \\(4104 + 54720 = 58824\\)\n     - \\(58824 + 273600 = 332424\\)\n\nThus, the final product of 684 and 486 is \\(\\boxed{332424}\\).",
