t I did. So that's correct. So the answer is 338,886. I think that's right. Let me just do a quick estimate to check if the magnitude makes sense. 400 \u00d7 800 is 320,000. 400\u00d7843 would be around 337,200, and 402 is a bit more, so 338,886 is reasonable. Yeah, that seems correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 402 and 843 is \\boxed{338886}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 402 and 843, we break down the multiplication by place value:\n\n1. **Multiply 402 by the ones place digit (3) of 843:**\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 3 = 1206\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 402 by the tens place digit (40) of 843:**\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 40 = 16080\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 402 by the hundreds place digit (800) of 843:**\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 800 = 321600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results from the steps above:\n\\[\n1206 + 16080 + 321600\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(1206\\) and \\(16080\\):\n\\[\n1206 + 16080 = 17286\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to \\(321600\\):\n\\[\n17286 + 321600 = 338886\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 402 and 843 is \\(\\boxed{338886}\\).",
