t of 473 and 402?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 402 has three digits, so we can break it down into hundreds, tens, and ones places.\n1. Multiply 473 by the ones place digit (2) of 402:\n   \\[\n   473 \\times 2 = 946\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 473 by the tens place digit (0) of 402. Since the tens digit is 0, this product is 0:\n   \\[\n   473 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 473 by the hundreds place digit (4) of 402. Since this is the hundreds place, we also multiply by 100:\n   \\[\n   473 \\times 4 = 1892 \\quad \\text{and then} \\quad 1892 \\times 100 = 189200\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n946 + 0 + 189200 = 190146\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{190146}.",
