28; then +4,800=74,528. Yep, same as before.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product is indeed 74,528.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 274 and 272 is \\boxed{74528}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 274 and 272, we can break down the multiplication step by step using the standard algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 274 by the ones place digit (2) of 272:**\n   \\[\n   274 \\times 2 = 548\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 274 by the tens place digit (70) of 272:**\n   \\[\n   274 \\times 70 = 274 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 1918 \\times 10 = 19180\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 274 by the hundreds place digit (200) of 272:**\n   \\[\n   274 \\times 200 = 274 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 548 \\times 100 = 54800\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n548 + 19180 + 54800\n\\]\n\nAdding these step by step:\n- First, add \\(548\\) and \\(19180\\):\n  \\[\n  548 + 19180 = 19728\n  \\]\n- Then, add the result to \\(54800\\):\n  \\[\n  19728 + 54800 = 74528\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 274 and 272 is \\(\\boxed{74528}\\).",
