st multiply by 6: 976×6=5,856\n\nThen multiply by 20: 976×20=19,520\n\nThen multiply by 200: 976×200=195,200\n\nAdding those together: 5,856 +19,520 =25,376; 25,376 +195,200 =220,576. So that's the same result.\n\nAlternatively, to confirm with another method, perhaps using the standard multiplication:\n\n   976\n\n× 226\n\n------------\n\nFirst line (6): 5856\n\nSecond line (20): 19520 (shifted one position)\n\nThird line (200): 195200 (shifted two positions)\n\nAdding them:\n\n     5856\n\n   +19520\n\n   +195200\n\n   -----------\n\n   Let me add 5856 +19520 first:\n\n5856 +19520:\n\n5856 +19520:\n\nLet me do 5856 + 19520:\n\n5856 + 19520:\n\nAdding 5000 +19000 =24000; 800 +500=1300; 50+20=70; 6+0=6. Wait that's not straightforward. Alternatively, 19520 +5000=24520, plus 856 is 25376. Then adding to 195,200:\n\n25376 +195200:\n\n25,376 +195,200 = 220,576. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, I think the final answer is 220,576. Wait, but to ensure there's no arithmetic mistake, perhaps do a quick estimation. 976 is nearly 1000, 226 is about 200. So 1000×200=200,000. But since 976 is 24 less than 1000, and 226 is 26 more than 200, the actual product should be a bit more than 200,000. 220,576 is reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps compute 976×226:\n\nLet me compute 1000×226 =226,000. Subtract 24×226. 24×200=4,800 and 24×26=624. So total subtraction: 4,800+624=5,424. So 226,000 -5,424=220,576. Yes, that matches. So that's another way to confirm. Therefore, the answer is indeed 220,576.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 976 and 226 is \\boxed{220576}.\n"]
