 by breaking down the multiplication into partial products based on the place values of the digits in 339.\n\n1. **Multiply 191 by the ones place digit (9) of 339:**\n   \\[\n   191 \\times 9 = 1719\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(9 \\times 1 = 9\\)\n     - \\(9 \\times 9 = 81\\) (write down 1, carry over 8)\n     - \\(9 \\times 1 = 9 + 8 = 17\\)\n   - Result: 1719\n\n2. **Multiply 191 by the tens place digit (30) of 339:**\n   \\[\n   191 \\times 30 = 5730\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(3 \\times 1 = 3\\)\n     - \\(3 \\times 9 = 27\\) (write down 7, carry over 2)\n     - \\(3 \\times 1 = 3 + 2 = 5\\)\n   - Result: 573 (shifted one position to the left: 5730)\n\n3. **Multiply 191 by the hundreds place digit (300) of 339:**\n   \\[\n   191 \\times 300 = 57300\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(3 \\times 1 = 3\\)\n     - \\(3 \\times 9 = 27\\) (write down 7, carry over 2)\n     - \\(3 \\times 1 = 3 + 2 = 5\\)\n   - Result: 573 (shifted two positions to the left: 57300)\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1719 + 5730 + 57300 = 64749\n   \\]\n   - Step-by-step addition:\n     - \\(1719 + 5730 = 7449\\)\n     - \\(7449 + 57300 = 64749\\)\n\nThus, the product of 191 and 339 is \\(\\boxed{64749}\\).",
