hould be 276,271.\n\nWait, but hold on, in my first calculation I thought of 256,400 +19,871 (which is 256,400 + 19,871). Let me compute 256,400 +19,871 again:\n\n256,400 +19,871:\n\n256,400 +10,000 =266,400\n\n266,400 +9,871 =276,271. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, adding the three numbers:\n\n641 +19,230 +256,400 = ?\n\nLet me add 641 +256,400 first: 257,041. Then add 19,230: 257,041 +19,230 = 276,271. Same result.\n\nTherefore, the product of 641 and 431 is indeed 276,271. I think that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe final computed product is \\boxed{276271}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 641 and 431, we break down the multiplication using the place values of 431:\n\n1. Multiply 641 by the ones place digit (1) of 431:\n   \\[\n   641 \\times 1 = 641\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 641 by the tens place digit (30) of 431:\n   \\[\n   641 \\times 30 = 641 \\times 3 \\times 10 = 1923 \\times 10 = 19230\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 641 by the hundreds place digit (400) of 431:\n   \\[\n   641 \\times 400 = 641 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 2564 \\times 100 = 256400\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n641 + 19230 + 256400\n\\]\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n1. First, add the ones and tens place results:\n   \\[\n   641 + 19230 = 19871\n   \\]\n\n2. Then add the result to the hundreds place result:\n   \\[\n   19871 + 256400 = 276271\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{276271}\\).",
