mes 4 = 1132\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(200 \\times 4 = 800\\), \\(80 \\times 4 = 320\\), \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\)\n   - Sum: \\(800 + 320 + 12 = 1132\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 283 by the tens place digit (90) of 894:**\n   \\[\n   283 \\times 90 = 25470\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(283 \\times 9 = 2547\\), then add a zero: \\(2547 \\times 10 = 25470\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 283 by the hundreds place digit (800) of 894:**\n   \\[\n   283 \\times 800 = 226400\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(283 \\times 8 = 2264\\), then add two zeros: \\(2264 \\times 100 = 226400\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1132 + 25470 + 226400\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(1132 + 25470\\):\n     \\[\n     1132 + 25470 = 26602\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(226400\\):\n     \\[\n     26602 + 226400 = 253002\n     \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 283 and 894 is \\(\\boxed{253002}\\).",
