t's count:.\n\nDigits of 203,200:  .\nHundred thousands: 2  .\nTen thousands:0  .\nThousands:3  .\nHundreds:2  .\nTens:0  .\nOnes:0  .\n\nDigits of 23,876:  .\nTen thousands:2  .\nThousands:3  .\nHundreds:8  .\nTens:7  .\nOnes:6  .\n\nWait, actually, perhaps aligning:.\n\n203200  .\n+\xa0 23876  .\n=  .\nSo:.\n\n203200  .\n+\xa0 23876  .\n_________  .\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 0 +6=6  .\nTens:0 +7=7  .\nHundreds:2 +8=10 → 0, carryover 1  .\nThousands:3 +3=6 plus 1 →7  .\nTen thousands:0 (from 203200's ten thousands place?) Wait, 203,200 has ten thousands digit as 0? Wait, 203,200 is 2 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones). So when adding to 23,876 which is 2 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 6 (ones). .\n\nSo the ten thousands place for 203200 is 0 (since it's 200,000 +3,200), so the ten thousands digit is 0. The ten thousands digit in 23,876 is 2. So adding ten thousands: 0 +2=2. .\n\nHundred thousands place: 2 (from 203,200) + 0 (from 23,876) =2. .\n\nPutting it all together: .\n\nHundred thousands: 2  .\nTen thousands:2  .\nThousands:7  .\nHundreds:0 (from the carryover)  .\nTens:7  .\nOnes:6  .\n\nWait, let me recheck:.\n\nAfter thousands place: 3 (from 203200's thousands digit) plus 3 (from 23,876's thousands digit) is 6 plus the carryover 1 makes 7. .\n\nThen ten thousands place: 0 (from 203200's ten thousands digit) + 2 (from 23,876's ten thousands digit) = 2.\n\nHundred thousands: 2 (from 203200) plus nothing, so 2. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
