  8\n\nAdding each column:\n\nOnes: 0 +8 =8\n\nTens:0 +6=6\n\nHundreds:6 +7=13 \u2192 write 3, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:0 +3 +1 (carry)=4, carryover 0.\n\nTen thousands:2 +3=5\n\nHundred thousands:1 +0=1.\n\nSo the total is 1 5 4 3 6 8 \u2192 154,368. Yes, that's correct. So the total is 154,368.\n\nWait, but let me cross-verify using another method to be sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using another multiplication approach.\n\nAlternatively, 402 \u00d7 384. Let me compute 400\u00d7384 + 2\u00d7384.\n\n400\u00d7384: 400\u00d7300 = 120,000; 400\u00d780=32,000; 400\u00d74=1,600. So total 120,000 +32,000 =152,000 +1,600 =153,600.\n\nThen 2\u00d7384=768. So total is 153,600 +768 =154,368. Yep, same result. Good, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard algorithm:\n\n       402\n     \u00d7384\n     -------\n       1608  (402 \u00d74)\n      32160  (402 \u00d780, shifted one position)\n    +120600  (402 \u00d7300, shifted two positions)\n     ---------\n     154368\n\nYes, that's exactly the same as before. So the answer is 154,368. I think that's correct. Let me check with a calculator maybe? Wait, since I can't use a calculator, but let me see another way.\n\nAlternatively, breaking down 384 into 400 - 16. So 402 \u00d7 (400 -16) = 402\u00d7400 -402\u00d716.\n\n402\u00d7400 = 160,800.\n\n402\u00d716: 400\u00d716=6,400; 2\u00d716=32 \u2192 total 6,432.\n\nSo 160,800 -6,432 = ?\n\n160,800 minus 6,000 is 154,800. Then subtract 432 more: 154,800 -432 =154,368. Yep, same result. So that's a good check. So I can be confident the answer is 154,368.\n\nSo following the template, the reasoning would be:\n\n1. Multiply 402 by 4 (the ones place digit of 384): 402 \u00d74 =1608.\n\n2. Multiply 402 by 80 (the tens place digit of 384): 402\u00d780=32,160.\n\n3. Multiply 402 by 300 (the hundreds place digit of 384):402\u00d7300=120,600.\n\nSum them all: 1608 +32,160 =33,768; then 33,768 +120,600 =154,368.\n\nSo the final answer is 154,368.\n</think>\n\n",
