96. So that's correct.\n\nHmm, so the final answer should be 374,296. I think that's right. Let me try multiplying another way for cross-verification. Maybe using the standard algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 767 by 488:\n\nFirst write 767\n\nx488\n\n--------\n\nMultiply 767 by 8: 6,136\n\nMultiply 767 by 80: 61,360 (shifted one position)\n\nMultiply 767 by 400: 306,800 (shifted two positions)\n\nAdding them:\n\n6,136\n\n61,360\n\n306,800\n\nTotal is indeed 6,136 +61,360 = 67,496; 67,496 +306,800 = 374,296. Yep, matches.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method like (700+67)*(400+88). Wait, maybe that's more complicated. But perhaps (767)*(488) can be written as 767*(500 -12). Let's see:\n\n767*(500 -12) = 767*500 -767*12.\n\n767*500 = 383,500.\n\n767*12 = 767*(10 +2) = 7,670 + 1,534 = 9,204.\n\nSo 383,500 -9,204 = 374,296. Same result. Okay, that confirms it. So the answer is correct.\n\nI think that's solid. So the product is 374,296.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 767 and 488 is \\boxed{374296}.\n"]
