 do 580 \u00d7777 as (500 +80) \u00d7 (700 +70 +7). Let's expand that.\n\nFirst, 500\u00d7700 = 350,000.\n\n500\u00d770 = 35,000.\n\n500\u00d77 = 3,500.\n\nThen 80\u00d7700 =56,000.\n\n80\u00d770 =5,600.\n\n80\u00d77 =560.\n\nAdding all those together:\n\n350,000 +35,000 =385,000.\n\n385,000 +3,500 =388,500.\n\n388,500 +56,000 =444,500.\n\n444,500 +5,600 =450,100.\n\n450,100 +560 =450,660. So that also gives the same result. Okay, so all methods are confirming that 450,660 is the correct answer. I think that's solid.\n\nWait, but just to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors in my steps. Let me go through each multiplication again.\n\nFirst step: 580 \u00d77.\n\n500\u00d77=3500, 80\u00d77=560. 3500+560=4060. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 580\u00d770. Since 70 is 7\u00d710, so 4060\u00d710=40,600. Correct.\n\nThird step: 580\u00d7700. 700 is 7\u00d7100, so 4060\u00d7100=406,000. Correct.\n\nAdding them:\n\n4060 +40,600 = 44,660.\n\n44,660 +406,000 = 450,660. Yep.\n\nAnother way: 406,000 +40,600 is 446,600. Then +4,060: 446,600 +4,000 is 450,600, plus 60 is 450,660. Correct.\n\nAlright, so I feel confident that the product of 580 and 777 is indeed 450,660. I've checked it multiple ways and each time arrived at the same answer. So that must be the right result.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 580 and 777 is \\boxed{450660}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 580 and 777, we break down 777 into its place values (700, 70, and 7) and multiply each part by 580, then sum the results.\n\n1. **Multiply 580 by the ones place digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   580 \\times 7 = 4060\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(500 \\times 7 = 3500\\) and \\(80 \\times 7 = 560\\), so \\(3500 + 560 = 4060\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 580 by the tens place digit (70):**\n   \\[\n   580 \\times 70 = 40600\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(580 \\times 7 = 4060\\), then multiply by 10: \\(4060 \\times 10 = 40600\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 580 by the hundreds place digit (700):**\n   \\[\n   580 \\times 700 = 406000\n   