iply 253 by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   253 \\times 4 = 1012\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 253 by the tens place digit (40):**\n   \\[\n   253 \\times 40 = 10120\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 253 by the hundreds place digit (200):**\n   \\[\n   253 \\times 200 = 50600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n1012 + 10120 + 50600\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the first two steps:\n\\[\n1012 + 10120 = 11132\n\\]\n\nThen add the result of the third step:\n\\[\n11132 + 50600 = 61732\n\\]\n\nThus, the final product of 253 and 244 is \\(\\boxed{61732}\\).",
