0 = 51,960\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(866 \\times 6 = 5,196\\)\n   - Multiply by 10: \\(5,196 \\times 10 = 51,960\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 866 by the hundreds place digit (100):**\n   \\[\n   866 \\times 100 = 86,600\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: Adding two zeros to 866 gives 86,600.\n\n**Sum all the results:**\n\\[\n7,794 + 51,960 + 86,600\n\\]\n\n- Adding the first two results:\n  \\[\n  7,794 + 51,960 = 59,754\n  \\]\n- Adding the third result:\n  \\[\n  59,754 + 86,600 = 146,354\n  \\]\n\nThus, the final product of 866 and 169 is \\(\\boxed{146354}\\).",
