e ones place digit 8 of 688:  \n   \\(767 \\times 8 = 6136\\).  \n2. Multiply 767 by the tens place digit 80 of 688:  \n   \\(767 \\times 80 = 61360\\).  \n3. Multiply 767 by the hundreds place digit 600 of 688:  \n   \\(767 \\times 600 = 460200\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(6136 + 61360 + 460200 = 527696\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is 527696.  \n\n\\boxed{527696}",
