\nSo (600 +17) ×502. That would be 600×502 +17×502.\n\nCompute 600×502: 600×500=300,000 and 600×2=1,200, so total 301,200.\n\nThen 17×502. Let's compute that: 17×500=8,500 and 17×2=34, so total 8,534.\n\nAdding 301,200 +8,534: 301,200 +8,000 is 309,200, then +534 gives 309,734. Same result. Okay, so that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, I think the answer is correct. The steps in the reasoning should be as follows:\n\nMultiply 617 by 2 (ones place) to get 1,234.\n\nMultiply 617 by 0 (tens place) which is 0, shifted one position left (but since it's zero, it doesn't contribute).\n\nMultiply 617 by 5 (hundreds place) which is 3,085, then shift two positions left to make it 308,500.\n\nAdding all together: 1,234 + 0 + 308,500 = 309,734. So that's the answer.\n\nI think that's thorough. I just need to present it in the template format as per the example given.\n"]
