ace)\n2. Multiply 646 by 10 (tens place)\n3. Multiply 646 by 500 (hundreds place)\nThen sum all three.\n\nHence the reasoning steps should list all three, then sum. In my previous thought process, I considered all three steps, so that's correct. The answer should be 334,628. I think that's right. Let me check with a calculator. Wait, maybe I can do a quick check using estimation. 600×500 is 300,000. 600×20 is 12,000, so 600×520 is 312,000. Then 46×500=23,000, so adding up, but perhaps that's not helpful. Alternatively, 646 ×500 is 323,000, and 646×18 is 11,628. So total 323k +11,628 is 334,628. Yep. Alright, I think that's correct.\n"]
