ication. Let's try breaking down 358 into 300 + 50 +8 again, which is the same as before, so it's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, compute using the standard algorithm step by step:\n\nMultiply 678 \u00d7 358:\n\nStart with the ones digit (8):\n\n678  \n\u00d7\u202f358  \n________  \n5,424 (this is 678\u00d78)  \n33,900 (this is 678\u00d750, written shifted one left)  \n203,400 (this is 678\u00d7300, shifted two left)  \n________  \nNow adding those three lines:  \n5,424  \n+33,900  \n=39,324  \nThen +203,400 = 242,724. \n\nYes, so that's correct. I don't see any errors in the steps. So the final product is 242,724. Therefore, the answer should be 242,724.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 678 and 358 is \\boxed{242724}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 678 and 358, we use the standard multiplication method by breaking it down into steps based on the place values of the digits in 358.\n\n1. **Multiply 678 by the ones place digit (8) of 358:**\n   \\[\n   678 \\times 8 = 5424\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(600 \\times 8 = 4800\\)\n     - \\(70 \\times 8 = 560\\)\n     - \\(8 \\times 8 = 64\\)\n     - Sum: \\(4800 + 560 + 64 = 5424\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 678 by the tens place digit (50) of 358:**\n   \\[\n   678 \\times 50 = 33900\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(678 \\times 5 = 3390\\)\n     - Add a zero: \\(3390 \\times 10 = 33900\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 678 by the hundreds place digit (300) of 358:**\n   \\[\n   678 \\times 300 = 203400\n   \\]\n   - Calculation steps:\n     - \\(678 \\times 3 = 2034\\)\n     - Add two zeros: \\(2034 \\times 100 = 203400\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   5424 + 33900 + 203400 = 242724\n   \\]\n   - Step-by-step addition:\n     - \\(5424 + 33900 = 39324\\)\n     - \\(39324 + 203400 = 242724\\)\n\nThus, the final product of 678 and 358 is \\(\\boxed{242724}\\).",
