timation to see if it's reasonable.\n\n800*300 = 240,000. 848 is 48 more than 800, and 331 is 31 more than 300. So, (800 +48)*(300+31) = 800*300 +800*31 +48*300 +48*31.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n800*300 = 240,000\n\n800*31 = 24,800\n\n48*300 =14,400\n\n48*31 = 1,488\n\nAdding all together: 240,000 +24,800 =264,800; +14,400 =279,200; +1,488 =280,688. So that matches exactly. So the answer must be 280,688. So I think that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 280,688.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 848 and 331?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 331 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 848 by the ones place digit (1):  \n   \\(848 \\times 1 = 848\\).\n2. Multiply 848 by the tens place digit (30):  \n   \\(848 \\times 30 = 25,\\!440\\).\n3. Multiply 848 by the hundreds place digit (300):  \n   \\(848 \\times 300 = 254,\\!400\\).\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(848 + 25,\\!440 + 254,\\!400 = 280,\\!688\\).\n\nAnswer:  \nThe final computed product is \\boxed{280688}.",
