17,800 +3,452 =521,252. Okay, so that's the same result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, let me try the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n\u2003\u2003604  \n\u00d7\u202f863  \n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \nFirst, multiply by 3 (ones place):  \n604 \u00d7 3 = 1,812  \n\nThen multiply by 6 (tens place, so shifted one position):  \n604 \u00d7 6 = 3,624 \u2192 but shifted one gives 36,240  \n\nThen multiply by 8 (hundreds place, shifted two positions):  \n604 \u00d7 8 = 4,832 \u2192 shifted two gives 483,200  \n\nNow add them all:  \n\u2003\u202f1,812  \n\u202f36,240  \n+483,200  \n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014  \nTotal: 1,812 +36,240 =38,052; 38,052 +483,200 =521,252.  \n\nYes, that matches. So the answer should be 521,252. I think that's correct. Let me just check with a calculator in my mind. 600*800=480,000, but the actual numbers are a bit higher. So 604 is 4 more than 600, and 863 is 63 more than 800. The cross terms would be 600*63 + 4*800 +4*63. Let me see: 600*63 =37,800; 4*800=3,200; 4*63=252. Adding all cross terms: 37,800+3,200=41,000 +252=41,252. Then total product is 480,000 +41,252=521,252. Yes, that's another way to confirm. So the answer is indeed 521,252.\n\nI think that's solid. All methods converge to the same result. So the reasoning steps are correct as I initially broke them down.\n</think>\n\n",
