 but just to make sure I didn't make a mistake in arithmetic somewhere. Let me do 580×144 another way. Maybe 580×144 = 580×(100+44) =580×100 +580×44. \n\nCalculating 580×44 first. 580×40=23,200 and 580×4=2,320. Adding those gives 23,200+2,320=25,520. Then adding to 58,000 gives 58,000+25,520=83,520. Yep. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard algorithm:\n\n\u2003\u2003580\n×\xa0144\n—————\nFirst line: 580×4 =2320\n\nSecond line: 580×40 =23,200 (shifted one position left)\n\nThird line:580×100=58,000 (shifted two positions left)\n\nAdding them up:\n\n2320\n\n+23200\n\n=25520\n\n25520 +58000=83520. \n\nYes, so that's correct. Alright, I think that's solid. So the answer is 83,520.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe final computed product is \\boxed{83520}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 580 and 144, we break down the multiplication step by step using the digits of 144 (1 hundred, 4 tens, and 4 ones):\n\n1. **Multiply 580 by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   580 \\times 4 = 2320\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 580 by the tens place digit (40):**\n   \\[\n   580 \\times 40 = 23200\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 580 by the hundreds place digit (100):**\n   \\[\n   580 \\times 100 = 58000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n2320 + 23200 + 58000\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the ones and tens place multiplications:\n\\[\n2320 + 23200 = 25520\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result of the hundreds place multiplication:\n\\[\n25520 + 58000 = 83520\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{83520}\\)."]
