t is 1 as well, which represents 100. So multiplying 564 by 100. That would be 56400. .\n\nNow I need to add all these partial products together: 564 (from ones) + 5640 (from tens) + 56400 (from hundreds). Let me do the addition step by step.\n\nFirst, add 564 and 5640. Adding those gives 564 + 5640 = 6204. Then add that to 56400. 6204 + 56400. Let's see, 6204 + 56,400. Hmm, 6204 + 56,400. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
