ing \\(1 \\times 10\\)) of 514:  \n   \\[\n   536 \\times 10 = 5,\\!360\n   \\]  \n3. Multiply 536 by the hundreds place digit **500** (since the hundreds digit is 5, representing \\(5 \\times 100\\)) of 514:  \n   \\[\n   536 \\times 500 = 268,\\!000\n   \\]  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\[\n2,\\!144 + 5,\\!360 + 268,\\!000 = 275,\\!504\n\\]  \nSo, the final computed product is **275,504**.",
