final_output:  ['\n\nTo find the product of 739 and 289, we can break down the multiplication into smaller steps by considering the place values of 289 (200, 80, and 9).\n\n1. **Multiply 739 by 200:**\n   \\[\n   739 \\times 200 = 739 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 1478 \\times 100 = 147800\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 739 by 80:**\n   \\[\n   739 \\times 80 = 739 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 5912 \\times 10 = 59120\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 739 by 9:**\n   \\[\n   739 \\times 9 = 6651\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three products:\n\\[\n147800 + 59120 + 6651\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(147800\\) and \\(59120\\):\n\\[\n147800 + 59120 = 206920\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to \\(6651\\):\n\\[\n206920 + 6651 = 213571\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 739 and 289 is \\(\\boxed{213571}\\).', "206,920 + 6,651. Let's do it step by step:\n\n206,920 + 6,000 = 212,920,\n\n212,920 + 651 = 213,571.\n\nWait, wait, that might be miscalculating. Let me check again:\n\n206,920 + 6,651:\n\nStart with 206,920.\n\nAdd 6,000 to get 212,920.\n\nThen add 651. 212,920 + 600 = 213,520,\n\nthen add 51: 213,520 + 51 = 213,571.\n\nYes, so total is 213,571.\n\nHmm, but let me verify if each multiplication was correct, because sometimes adding up can lead to errors.\n\nFirst part: 739 × 200 = 147,800. That's correct because 700×200=140,000 and 39×200=7,800, so total 147,800.\n\nSecond part: 739×80. Let me recalculate that. 700×80=56,000, and 39×80=3,120. Adding them gives 56,000 + 3,120 = 59,120. Correct.\n\nThird part: 739×9. 700×9=6,300, 39×9=351, so total 6,651. Correct.\n\nAdding all three: 147,800 + 59,120 is indeed 206,920, then plus 6,651 gives 213,571. Hmm, that seems right. But let me cross-verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 739 × 289.\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n     739\n×  289\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 739 by 9 (the ones place):\n\n739 × 9: 9×9=81, write down 1 and carryover 8.\n\n9×3=27 +8=35, write