n739 ×2 =1,478 shifted left by two digits becomes 147,800.\n\nAdding:\n\n6,651\n\n59,120\n\n147,800\n\nLet me add 6,651 + 59,120 first. 6,651 +59,120: 6,000 +59,000 =65,000. 651 +120 =771. So total is 65,771. Then adding 147,800: 65,771 +147,800.\n\n65,771 +100,000 =165,771.\n\n165,771 +47,800 = 213,571. Yes, same result.\n\nOkay, I'm pretty confident now that the product is 213,571. So the answer should be 213,571.\n\nWait, but hold on, just to make sure I didn't make a mistake in any of the multiplication steps. Let me verify the first multiplication again: 739 ×200. 200 is two hundreds. 739×2=1,478, so 1,478×100 is 147,800. Correct.\n\nSecond, 739×80: 739×8 is 5,912, so times 10 is 59,120. Correct.\n\nThird, 739×9=6,651. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 147,800 +59,120 =206,920. Then +6,651: 206,920 +6,000 is 212,920, plus 651 is 213,571. All steps check out.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 213,571. I think that's correct. I don't see any errors in the calculations, and cross-verified with different methods.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 739 and 289 is \\boxed{213571}.\n"] 88%|########8 | 440/500 [6:05:31<1:05:04, 65.08s/it]
