ent.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use distributive property differently. Let me check with a calculator approach. Wait, since I can't use a calculator, but let me see:\n\nAlternatively, compute 400×565 + 1×565. Since 401 = 400 +1.\n\nSo, 400×565 = (4×565) ×100. 4×565 is 2260, so ×100 is 226,000.\n\nThen 1×565 = 565. So total is 226,000 +565 = 226,565. Oh! That's a smarter way. That also gives the same result. So that confirms it again. So that's good.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 226,565. I think that's correct. All methods lead to the same result. So I can be confident.\n\nWait, let me do the 400×565 again. 4×565 is indeed 2260, so 2260×100 is 226,000. Then adding 565 gives 226,565. Yep. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, if I do 565 × 400: 565 ×4 is 2260, so ×100 is 226,000. Then 565×1 is 565. So total is 226,565. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 226,565. All methods cross-check and confirm. I think that's solid.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 401 and 565 is \\boxed{226565}.\n"]
