.\n\n2,961 +23,030:\n\n2,000 +23,000 =25,000\n\n961 +30 =991\n\nTotal 25,991.\n\nThen add 197,400 to that:\n\n25,991 +197,400 = 223,391. So same result. Okay, so that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method like the distributive property:\n\n(300 +29) × (600 +79) ?\n\nHmm, maybe that complicates more. Alternatively, use calculator verification? Since I can't actually use a calculator, but I can check another way.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check if 329 ×679 is equal to (330 -1)×679 = 330×679 -679.\n\n330×679: 330×600=198,000; 330×79= ?\n\n330×70=23,100; 330×9=2,970; so total 23,100+2,970=26,070. So total 198,000 +26,070 =224,070.\n\nThen subtract 679: 224,070 -679 =223,391. So same answer. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product is 223,391.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 329 and 679 is \\boxed{223391}.\n"]
