tial product.\n\nNow, I need to add all three partial products together: 1775 + 24,850 + 106,500. Let me add the first two first. 1775 + 24,850. Let's see, 1775 + 24,850. 24,850 + 1,000 is 25,850, then subtract 225 (since 1775 is 1000 + 775, but maybe easier to do straight addition). Alternatively, 24,850 + 1,775: 24,850 + 1,000 is 25,850; 25,850 + 700 is 26,550; then +75 gives 26,625. Wait, maybe I miscalculated. Let me check again:.\n\n24,850  .\n+  1,775  .\n=  .\n24,850 + 1,000 = 25,850  .\n25,850 + 700 = 26,550  .\n26,550 + 75 = 26,625. Yes, that's right.\n\nNow add the third partial product: 26,625 + 106,500. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
