at can't be. Wait, 485,600 + 42,490: 485,600 + 40,000 = 525,600; 525,600 + 2,490 = 528,090. Then add 5,463: 528,090 + 5,463 = 533,553. Yes, that's the same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 607 × 879 directly using another method. Let's see:\n\n607 × 879 = 607 × (800 + 70 +9) = 607×800 + 607×70 + 607×9, which is exactly what I did. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, to confirm, maybe using calculator-like steps:\n\nMultiply 607 by 879:\n\nFirst, 607 × 9 = 5,463.\n\nThen 607 ×70: 607×7=4,249, so ×10 is 42,490.\n\nThen 607×800= 607×8×100=4,856×100=485,600.\n\nAdding all those gives 5,463 +42,490 = 47,953; 47,953 +485,600=533,553.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 533,553. I think that's correct. Let me just verify once more with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property in another way. Let's see, 607 × 879 can be thought of as (600 +7)(800 +70 +9). Expanding this would give 600×800 + 600×70 +600×9 +7×800 +7×70 +7×9. Then adding all those terms:\n\n600×800 = 480,000\n\n600×70 =42,000\n\n600×9 =5,400\n\n7×800=5,600\n\n7×70=490\n\n7×9=63\n\nNow add all these up:\n\n480,000 +42,000 = 522,000\n\n522,000 +5,400 = 527,400\n\n527,400 +5,600 = 533,000\n\n533,000 +490 =533,490\n\n533,490 +63=533,553. \n\nYes, same result. So that's a good check. Therefore, the answer is indeed 533,553. I think that's correct. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Each step checks out when approached different ways. So I'm confident the product is 533,553.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 607 and 879 is \\boxed{533553}.\n"]
