o 276,300:\n\n276,300  \n+31,314  \n=?\n\n276,300 + 31,314:\n\n200,000 + 70,000 +6,300 + 31,314. Hmm, maybe better step by step.\n\n276,300 + 30,000 = 306,300  \n306,300 + 1,314 = 307,614. Correct.\n\nAlright, seems consistent. I think that's the right answer. So the product of 921 and 334 is 307,614.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 921 and 334 is \\boxed{307614}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 921 and 334, we break down the multiplication by place value:\n\n1. **Ones place (4):**  \n   \\( 921 \\times 4 = 3684 \\)\n\n2. **Tens place (30):**  \n   \\( 921 \\times 30 = 27630 \\)\n\n3. **Hundreds place (300):**  \n   \\( 921 \\times 300 = 276300 \\)\n\nNext, we sum the results of each step:  \n\\[\n3684 + 27630 + 276300\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the ones and tens results:  \n\\[\n3684 + 27630 = 31314\n\\]\n\nThen add the hundreds result:  \n\\[\n31314 + 276300 = 307614\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 921 and 334 is \\(\\boxed{307614}\\).",
