=320;7\u00d78=56. 7,200+320=7,520; 7,520+56=7,576. Correct.\n\nSecond: 947\u00d780. Since 80 is 8\u00d710, so 7,576 \u00d710=75,760. Correct.\n\nThird:947\u00d7900. 900 is 9\u00d7100. 947\u00d79=8,523. Then \u00d7100 gives 852,300. Correct.\n\nAdding all three gives the total. So the answer is indeed 935,636.\n\nHmm, so the problem is solved correctly. I think that's it.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 947 and 988 is \\boxed{935636}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 947 and 988, we break it down into partial products based on the digits of 988:\n\n1. **Multiply 947 by the ones place digit (8):**\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 8 = 7576\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - \\(900 \\times 8 = 7200\\)\n   - \\(40 \\times 8 = 320\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 8 = 56\\)\n   - Summing these: \\(7200 + 320 + 56 = 7576\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 947 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 80 = 75760\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - \\(947 \\times 8 = 7576\\)\n   - Shifting one position left (multiplying by 10): \\(7576 \\times 10 = 75760\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 947 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 900 = 852300\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - \\(947 \\times 9 = 8523\\)\n   - Shifting two positions left (multiplying by 100): \\(8523 \\times 100 = 852300\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   7576 + 75760 + 852300\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(7576\\) and \\(75760\\):\n     \\[\n     7576 + 75760 = 83336\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(852300\\):\n     \\[\n     83336 + 852300 = 935636\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 947 and 988 is \\(\\boxed{935636}\\).",
