ace) +8 (ten thousands?) Wait need to align properly.\n\nWait maybe better to add 852,300 +83,336:\n\n852,300 + 83,336 = (852,300 + 80,000) + 3,336 = 932,300 + 3,336 = 935,636.\n\nYes, so total is 935,636.\n\nWait, so the final product should be 935,636?\n\nWait, let me check using another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard algorithm.\n\nAlternatively, compute 947 × 988.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use the distributive property: (900 + 40 +7) × (900 +80 +8). But that might be more complex, but let me try.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use (947)(988) = 947*(1000 - 12) since 988 is 1000 -12.\n\nSo, 947*1000 - 947*12 = 947,000 - 11,364 = ?\n\n947,000 -11,364:.\n\n947,000 minus 10,000 is 937,000. Then minus 1,364 more: 937,000 -1,364 = 935,636. Same result. So that's good.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 935,636.\n\nWait, but let me check again the partial products:\n\nFirst partial product: 947×8 =7,576.\n\nSecond: 947×80=75,760.\n\nThird:947×900=852,300.\n\nAdding those:7,576 +75,760 = 83,336. Then 83,336 +852,300 =935,636. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made a mistake in the initial steps? Let me verify each partial product again.\n\nFirst: 947 ×8.\n\n900×8=7,200; 40×8=320;7×8=56. 7,200+320=7,520; 7,520+56=7,576. Correct.\n\nSecond: 947×80. Since 80 is 8×10, so 7,576 ×10=75,760. Correct.\n\nThird:947×900. 900 is 9×100. 947×9=8,523. Then ×100 gives 852,300. Correct.\n\nAdding all three gives the total. So the answer is indeed 935,636.\n\nHmm, so the problem is solved correctly. I think that's it.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 947 and 988 is \\boxed{935636}.\n"]
