r**\nThe product of 468 and 638 is \\boxed{298584}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 468 and 638, we break down the multiplication into parts based on the digits of 638:\n\n1. **Multiply 468 by the ones place digit (8):**\n   \\[\n   468 \\times 8 = 3744\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   400 \\times 8 = 3200, \\quad 60 \\times 8 = 480, \\quad 8 \\times 8 = 64\n   \\]\n   Summing these results:\n   \\[\n   3200 + 480 + 64 = 3744\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 468 by the tens place digit (30):**\n   \\[\n   468 \\times 30 = 14040\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   468 \\times 3 = 1404 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 468 by the hundreds place digit (600):**\n   \\[\n   468 \\times 600 = 280800\n   \\]\n   Calculation:\n   \\[\n   468 \\times 6 = 2808 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   3744 + 14040 + 280800\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(3744\\) and \\(14040\\):\n     \\[\n     3744 + 14040 = 17784\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(280800\\):\n     \\[\n     17784 + 280800 = 298584\n     \\]\n\n### Answer:\nThe product of 468 and 638 is \\(\\boxed{298584}\\).",
