place contribution (229), the tens (2290), and the hundreds (68,700). Let me write them down:.\n\n229 (from 1).\n+2290 (from 10).\n+68700 (from 300).\n----------.\n\nAdding the first two: 229 + 2290. Let's see, 229 + 2000 is 2229, then plus 290 more? Wait, no, that's not right. Wait, 229 + 2290. Let me do it step by step. 229 + 2290. The 229 is in the ones place, and 2290 is shifted one position to the left because it's the tens place. Wait, actually, in the standard multiplication, each subsequent multiplication is shifted left by one digit, so when adding, their places are already considered. Wait, maybe I need to think of each step as already in their correct places. Let me clarify.\n\nWait, actually, in the standard algorithm, when you multiply by the ones digit, you write the result as is. When you multiply by the tens digit, you shift one place to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 10), and the hundreds digit multiplication shifts two places (equivalent to multiplying by 100). So adding them would be:.\n\n229 × 1 = 229 (ones place).\n229 × 10 = 2290 (tens place, so shifted one).\n229 × 300 = 68700 (hundreds place, shifted two).\nSo adding them together:.\n\n   229.\n+ 2290.\n+68700.\n--------.\nLet me line them up properly:.\n\n    229.\n   2290.\n+68700.\n--------.\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\nThe ones place: 9 + 0 + 0 =9.\nTens place: 2 +9 +0 =11, carry over 1.\nHundreds place: 2 (from 229) + 2 (from 2290) +7 (from 68700) plus the carried 1. Wait, let me see:.\n\nWait, maybe I should write them vertically aligned:.\n\n       229.\n      2290.\n    +68700.\n    ---------.\nAdding these:.\n\nStart with the units column: 9 (from 229) + 0 (from 2290) + 0 (from 68700) =9.\n\nTens column: 2 (from 229) +9 (from 2290) +0 (from 68700) =11. So write 1, carry over 1.\n\nHundreds column: 2 (from 229) +2 (from 2290) +7 (from 68700) +1 (carry) = 12. So write 2, carry over 1.\n\nThousands column: 0 (from 229) +6 (from 68700) + the carried 1 =7.\n\nTen-thousands column: 6 (from 68700) remains.\n\nWait, maybe I'm miscalculating the columns. Let me write each number with commas to see:.\n\n229 is 0000229.\n\n2290 is 0002290.\n\n68700 is 068700.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nUnits place: 9 +0 +0 =9.\n\nTens: 2 +9 +0 =11 → 1, carry 1.\n\nHundreds: 2 +2 +7 =11 plus the carry 1 makes 12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 0 (from 229) + 2 (from 2290) +8 (from 68700) plus carry 1 → 2+8=10 +1=11 → 1, carry 1.\n\nTen-thousands: 6 (from 68700) plus carry 1 →7.\n\nHundred-thousands: 0 +0 +0 =0, but the 6 in 68700 is in the ten-thousands place. Wait, maybe my breakdown is off. Let's do it step by step numerically:.\n\n229.\n\n+2290 = 229 + 2290 = 2519. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]] 93%|#########3| 467/500 [6:29:16<26:24, 48.03s/it]
