      "text": "229 \u00d7 311 = 229*(300+10+1)=229*300 +229*10 +229*1 = 68700 + 2290 +229.\n\nCalculating 68700 +2290: 68700 + 2000 =70700, plus 290 is 70990. Then add 229 to that: 70990 +229 = 71219. Wait, is that right?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\n68700 +2290 = 68700 + 2000 =70700, then +290 =70990. Then 70990 +229. Let's do 70990 +200 =71190, plus 29 =71219.\n\nHmm, but let me verify using another method. Let me do 229 \u00d7 311 directly.\n\nAlternatively, 229 \u00d7 311 can be computed as (200 +29) \u00d7 (300 +11). But maybe that complicates. Alternatively, use the standard multiplication:\n\n   229\n\u00d7 311\n--------\nFirst, multiply 229 by 1 (units place): 229.\n\nThen multiply 229 by 1 (tens place): 229 shifted one left \u21922290.\n\nThen multiply 229 by 3 (hundreds place): 229\u00d73=687, shifted two left \u219268700.\n\nNow adding them:\n\n229 +2290 = 2519; then 2519 +68700 =71219. So that's the same result as before. So the product should be 71,219.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another approach. Let me compute 229 \u00d7 311 using another method to cross-verify.\n\nAlternatively, 311 \u00d7229.\n\nLet me compute 311 \u00d7200 =62,200.\n\n311 \u00d729: 311\u00d730=9,330 minus 311 gives 9,330 -311 =9,019.\n\nSo total is 62,200 +9,019 =71,219. Same result. Okay, that matches. So I think 71,219 is correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 71,219. Let me make sure there are no arithmetic errors in the steps. The step-by-step breakdown seems consistent. So the final answer is 71219.\n\n</think>\n\n",
