\\(356 \\times 3 = 1068\\), then add a zero: \\(1068 \\times 10 = 10680\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 356 by the hundreds place digit (500):**\n   \\[\n   356 \\times 500 = 178000\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(356 \\times 5 = 1780\\), then add two zeros: \\(1780 \\times 100 = 178000\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   2136 + 10680 + 178000 = 190816\n   \\]\n   - Step-by-step addition:\n     - \\(178000 + 10680 = 188680\\)\n     - \\(188680 + 2136 = 190816\\)\n\nThus, the final product of 356 and 536 is \\(\\boxed{190816}\\).",
