 and 536?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 536 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps:\n1. Multiply 794 by the ones place digit 6 of 536:\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 6 = 4764\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 794 by the tens place digit 30 of 536:\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 30 = 23820\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 794 by the hundreds place digit 500 of 536:\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 500 = 397000\n   \\]\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n4764 + 23820 + 397000 = 425584\n\\]\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{425584}.",
