 + 967\u00d71 = same as above. So same steps.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check using another method like the lattice method or cross-multiplication, but that might be time-consuming. Alternatively, approximate to see if the answer is reasonable.\n\nLet me approximate the numbers to check. 967 is close to 1000, and 921 is close to 900. So 1000 \u00d7 900 = 900,000. The actual product should be a bit less than that, since 967 is 33 less than 1000, and 921 is 79 more than 900. Hmm, but maybe the approximation isn't straightforward. Alternatively, 967 \u00d7 921: Let's see, 967 \u00d7 900 = 870,300, then 967 \u00d7 21 = ?\n\nWait, 967 \u00d721 = 967\u00d720 + 967\u00d71 = 19,340 + 967 = 20,307. Then total is 870,300 +20,307 = 890,607. Same result. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator? But since I can't, I have to rely on my calculations.\n\nWait, another way: Let me reverse the multiplication. 921 \u00d7 967. Let's see if that gives the same result. Let me try.\n\nFirst, 921 \u00d7 7 (the ones place of 967):\n\n921 \u00d77 = 6,447.\n\nThen 921 \u00d760 (the tens place, which is 60):\n\n921 \u00d760 = 55,260.\n\nThen 921 \u00d7900 (the hundreds place):\n\n921 \u00d7900 = 828,900.\n\nNow add them up: 6,447 +55,260 = 61,707. Then 61,707 +828,900 = 890,607. Same result! So that's a good check.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the answer is 890,607.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 967 and 921 is \\boxed{890607}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 967 and 921, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. Multiply 967 by the ones place digit (1) of 921:\n   \\[\n   967 \\times 1 = 967\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 967 by the tens place digit (20) of 921:\n   \\[\n   967 \\times 20 = 19,340\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 967 by the hundreds place digit (900) of 921:\n   \\[\n   967 \\times 900 = 870,300\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n967 + 19,340 + 870,300\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 967 and 19,340:\n\\[\n967 + 19,340 = 20,307\n\\]\n\