atively, perhaps use the fact that (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd, but that might complicate here. Alternatively, maybe approximate to check if the answer is reasonable.\n\nLet me see: 491 is close to 500, and 921 is close to 900. So 500 × 900 = 450,000. The actual answer should be a bit more than that because both numbers are slightly higher than 500 and 900. Wait, 491 is 9 less than 500, and 921 is 21 more than 900. So, the exact calculation would be (500 -9)(900 +21) = 500×900 + 500×21 -9×900 -9×21. Let's compute that:\n\n500×900 = 450,000  \n500×21 = 10,500  \n9×900 = 8,100  \n9×21 = 189  \n\nSo, total is 450,000 +10,500 = 460,500; minus (8,100 +189)=8,289. So 460,500 -8,289 = ?\n\n460,500 - 8,000 = 452,500  \nThen subtract 289 more: 452,500 -289 = 452,211. \n\nWait, that's the same answer as before! So that cross-verification using the distributive property gives me the same result. That's reassuring. So the answer must be 452,211.\n\nHmm, so all my methods are leading me to 452,211. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 491 and 921 is indeed 452,211.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 491 and 921 is \\boxed{452211}.\n"]
