 as in the standard algorithm to confirm:\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n       117  \n     \u00d7563  \n     -------\nFirst multiply by 3:  \n117 \u00d7 3 = 351. So first partial product: 351.\n\nNext, multiply by 6 (tens place, so actually 60).  \n117 \u00d7 6 = 702. Then shift one position to the left: 7020. Second partial product: 7020.\n\nThen multiply by 5 (hundreds place, so 500).  \n117 \u00d75 = 585. Shift two positions left: 58500. Third partial product: 58500.\n\nAdd them all together: 351 +7020 = 7371; 7371 +58500 = 65871. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use a calculator to confirm, but since I can't, let me try another verification.\n\nAlternatively, compute 117 \u00d7 560 + 117 \u00d73.\n\nBecause 563 is 560 +3.\n\n117 \u00d7560: Let's compute 117 \u00d756 \u00d710.\n\nFirst compute 117 \u00d756.\n\n117 \u00d756: Break it down as (100 +17) \u00d756.\n\n100\u00d756 =5600, 17\u00d756. Let's compute 17\u00d750=850, 17\u00d76=102. So 850+102=952. So total 5600+952=6552. Then \u00d710 gives 65520.\n\nThen add 117\u00d73=351. So total is 65520 +351= 65871. Same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product is 65,871.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 117 and 563 is \\boxed{65871}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 117 and 563, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of 563.\n\n1. **Multiply 117 by the ones place digit (3) of 563:**\n   \\[\n   117 \\times 3 = 351\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 117 by the tens place digit (60) of 563:**\n   \\[\n   117 \\times 60 = 117 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 702 \\times 10 = 7020\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 117 by the hundreds place digit (500) of 563:**\n   \\[\n   117 \\times 500 = 117 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 585 \\times 100 = 58500\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these partial products:\n\\[\n351 + 7020 + 58500\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 351 and 7020:\n\\[\n351 + 7020 = 7371\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to 58500:\n\\[\n7371 + 58500 = 65871\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product