d left → 00 (but still 0).\n\nThird digit (hundreds): 7, so 904 ×7 shifted two positions left (multiply by 100). .\n\nTherefore, the steps would be:.\n\n1. 904 × 0 = 0.\n\n2. 904 × 0 (tens place, so 0 ×10 → but written as 0 shifted left by 1 → but since it's 0, still 0).\n\n3. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
